const n=[{slug:"ngan-sach-website-nam-dau",title:"First year website budget: how to allocate between construction and operation?",metaTitle:"First year website budget: construction and operation allocation | Xartisan Studio",description:"How to set a website budget for the first 12 months: separate investment in construction, infrastructure, operations, content, advertising and backup, then allocate according to the website's role in business.",keywords:["Website budget","first year website costs","Set up a website budget","website operating costs"],category:"Costs & quotes",tags:["Budget","Cost","Operations"],date:"2026-10-10",updated:"2026-10-11",readingMinutes:9,excerpt:"Many businesses spend most of their budget on creating a website and then have nothing left to operate. The article suggests how to divide the budget for the first 12 months according to goals, so that the website really works after the handover date.",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","chi-phi-an-khi-lam-website-gia-re"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"When planning to build a website, the most familiar question is: how much does it cost to build a website? The more accurate question is: **How ​​much does it take in the first 12 months for the website to be both built properly and have people operating it to bring in customers**. Website is an asset. The new handover date is the date the asset begins working; If the entire budget is spent on construction, the asset will stand still and gradually deteriorate. This article helps you divide your first year budget into clear sections and allocate them according to your business goals."},{type:"h2",text:"Why should you create a budget for the entire first year?"},{type:"p",text:"A newly launched website has no rankings, no data, and not many people know about it. The first months are the period that requires the most work: adding content, fixing common stumbling points, tracking data and making adjustments. If the budget is only enough for the construction part, the website falls into a familiar scenario: beautiful at handover, then no one updates, no one measures and almost no customers."},{type:"p",text:"Creating a yearly budget helps you see the true nature: **cost of website ownership** includes the initial investment plus all costs to maintain and develop it. Comparing options based on website price alone often leads to a choice that is cheap at first but expensive later."},{type:"h2",text:"6 items needed in the first year website budget"},{type:"table",headers:["Clause","Properties","What's included?","Note"],rows:[["Construction investment (Setup)","Once","Clarify goals, content structure, design, programming, platform technical SEO, and measurement settings","Clearly state the scope to avoid problems"],["Infrastructure","Every year","Domain name, hosting or server, email domain name if needed","Register in the name of the business, turn on automatic renewal"],["Monthly operations","Periodically","Monitor, backup, update, troubleshoot, report","Keep assets from deteriorating"],["Content and SEO","Periodically","New articles, service pages, images, optimized according to search queries","It takes time to see results"],["Advertisement (if any)","According to the campaign","The budget pays for Google, Meta, TikTok and other platforms","Separate from operating fees"],["Backup","When needed","New features, seasonal campaigns, adjustments to new regulations","There should be, no matter how small"]]},{type:"p",text:"The two most easily forgotten items are operations and backup. Without them, every change in the first year becomes an unexpected expense, and the website is easily abandoned right when it needs the most care."},{type:"h2",text:"Principle of allocation: don't put it all into construction"},{type:"ul",items:["**Build just enough, build right**: prioritize pages and features that directly generate contacts and orders. The \"nice to have\" feature goes to a later stage, when real data is available.","**Retain budget for at least 12 months of operation**: this is an amount that helps prevent the website from being abandoned after handover.","**Separate advertising from operations**: money paid to the advertising platform should be a separate line, so you know clearly how much goes into maintaining assets and how much goes into attracting customers.","**Always have a reserve**: every first year there are unforeseen things, like adding a service page, a landing page for peak season or adjusting to new regulations."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Quick rules when on a tight budget",text:"Minimize the scope of construction, not the operation. A website with few pages but well taken care of often brings in more visitors than a large website that is neglected."},{type:"h2",text:"Allocation by website role: three common scenarios"},{type:"p",text:"There is no common rate for all businesses. The reasonable division depends on the role of the website in the business. The table below describes the relative priority between items, not a fixed number."},{type:"table",headers:["Role of website","Construction","Operations","Content and SEO","Advertisement"],rows:[["Capacity profile for partners to evaluate","Cao","Medium","Low to moderate","Low or no"],["Channel to find new customers through Google","Medium","Medium","Cao","Depends on stage"],["Main sales channel","Cao","Cao","Medium to high","Cao"]]},{type:"p",text:"Capacity profile website needs careful investment at construction: standard information, real images, clear project; The main operation is to keep information always correct and the website always safe. Websites that find customers through Google need regular, long-term content and SEO. When the website is the main sales channel, everything is important and should be measured by orders and revenue."},{type:"h2",text:"Suggested spending schedule for the first 12 months"},{type:"ol",items:["**Before launch**: finalize scope, prepare content and images, build, test, set measurements. This is the phase where the largest investment is spent.","**January to March**: closely monitor data, fix points that visitors often leave, add missing content, submit sitemap and check index on Google Search Console.","**April to June**: gradually increase content and SEO according to queries that appear, try landing pages for key products or services.","**July to December**: focus budget on channels and pages that have proven effective, cut back on what doesn't bring in customers.","**End of year**: summarize costs per contact or order to create a second year budget."]},{type:"h2",text:"Mistakes cause website budget to be wasted"},{type:"ul",items:["Choose the cheapest option for construction, then spend money repairing it again and again or having to redo it after only a year or two.","Do not specify the scope, so that every small change becomes an additional expense.","Run ads when the website has no measurement, so you don't know how much money it brings in customers.","If you leave the domain name or hosting in someone else's name, when you change the unit, you have to pay extra to get it back.","Completely cut off operations immediately after launch, right when the website needed the most care."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Ask clearly before signing",text:"Require the web company to separate which amounts are one-time expenses, which are recurring expenses, which are paid to third parties, and what the warranty policy includes. The article [hidden costs when building a cheap website](/blog/cost-phi-an-when-making-website-gia-re) lists items that are often overlooked."},{type:"h2",text:"How does the monthly Setup plus operation model help the budget?"},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio separates costs into two parts, exactly the way an asset is created and maintained. **Setup Package** is a one-time investment to build the foundation: clarifying goals, content structure, design, programming, platform technical SEO, measurement settings and handing over 100% ownership. Then the business chooses the appropriate monthly operating level: **Basic** to preserve assets, **Growth** to develop assets with regular content and SEO, **Performance** when the website is the main revenue growth channel."},{type:"p",text:"This method of division helps you know in advance which expenses are a one-time expense, which expenses are spent evenly each month, and choose the operating level according to the right stage of your business. Specific costs are reported separately after Xartisan Studio understands the goals and current status, because there is no general number that is correct for all businesses. See [monthly Setup and Operation Package model](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website) or read again [what does the website design cost include](/blog/cost-phi-thiet-ke-website)."},{type:"p",text:"A good budget is not the lowest budget, but the budget that helps the website continue to work after the handover date. If you are planning for next year, please [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) or text WhatsApp 0435 878 929 to share the budget according to your business goals."}],faq:[{question:"How much should be spent in the first year on operations versus construction?",answer:"There is no general rate. Capacity profile websites often focus more on construction, while websites that find customers through Google or sell products need to spend a significant part on operations, content and SEO. The safe rule is to always keep the budget for at least 12 months of operation."},{question:"If your budget is small, which part should you cut first?",answer:"You should reduce the scope of the project first, for example reducing extra features or making fewer pages, instead of cutting the operating part. A small website that is well taken care of can still be gradually expanded once it has customers."},{question:"Are advertising costs included in the operating package?",answer:"Are not. The budget paid for the advertising platform is always separate. Xartisan Studio's Performance package includes advertising operations leading to the website, but does not include an advertising budget."},{question:"Why doesn't Xartisan Studio report a general number for the first year's budget?",answer:"Because budget depends on goals, number of pages, features, available content and desired performance level. Xartisan Studio discusses first, then sends a separate quote clearly stating which expenses are one-time and which are recurring."},{question:"From the second year will website costs decrease?",answer:"The Setup package is only a one-time investment, so from the second year there is mainly infrastructure and operations left. Operating levels should be reviewed each year according to the business's growth goals."}]},{slug:"bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi",title:"What does website maintenance include? Monthly operational checklist for businesses",metaTitle:"What does website maintenance include? Monthly Checklist 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"What does website maintenance include, how often is it done, and how is it different from warranty? Checklist operates weekly, monthly, quarterly, and annually to help prevent business websites from degrading over time.",keywords:["website maintenance","What does website maintenance include?","Website maintenance checklist","Operate website monthly"],category:"Operations & security",tags:["Maintenance","Operations","Checklist"],date:"2026-09-29",updated:"2026-10-02",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"A website rarely crashes suddenly, it degrades slowly: it slows down, the form has errors without anyone knowing, the content gets old. This is a weekly, monthly, quarterly and annual maintenance checklist to keep assets in good condition.",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["bao-mat-website-ssl-sao-luu-cap-nhat","do-luong-website-ga4-search-console"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many businesses only remember their website when something happens: the page cannot be accessed, the customer reports that the form was not sent, or the browser shows an unsafe warning. In fact, websites rarely fail suddenly. It degrades slowly: speed slows down, software gets old, content gets outdated, links break, and every month it loses a few customers without anyone noticing. **Website maintenance** is a periodic task to prevent that process, just like maintaining a valuable asset."},{type:"h2",text:"What is website maintenance and how is it different from warranty?"},{type:"p",text:"Maintenance is **proactive, recurring scheduled work** to keep the website running stably, safely and with correct information: monitoring, backing up, updating, checking and reporting. Warranty is **the web company's commitment to what has been delivered**. These two concepts complement each other, not replace each other: warranty stands behind the quality of what is done, while maintenance keeps assets from deteriorating over time."},{type:"p",text:"For example, with Xartisan Studio, the warranty policy includes free correction within the accepted scope for 5 years (60 months) and a lifetime warranty against errors caused by Xartisan Studio; New features or changes beyond the scope of the cost are quoted in advance. For details, see page [warranty and handover](/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website). Besides, things like daily website monitoring, periodic backups, and monthly reports fall under the operations section."},{type:"h2",text:"Why does the website need regular maintenance?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Software is always changing**: browsers, libraries, plugins, PHP or Node.js versions are constantly updated. A website that stands still for a few years will gradually deviate from the environment in which it is running.","**Frequently announced security vulnerabilities**: slow software updates are the easiest targets for automated attacks.","**Silent error**: form cannot send email, WhatsApp button has wrong number, out of stock product is still displayed. No one announced, but the guests quietly left.","**Changed business information**: new policies, address, phone number, team, projects. Websites that say wrong information make customers lose trust faster than websites that lack information.","**Google continuously re-evaluates**: slow pages, index errors or old content may gradually drop in rankings without warning."]},{type:"h2",text:"Website maintenance checklist by frequency"},{type:"p",text:"The table below is the minimum set of tasks for a business or sales website. Large websites, with member accounts or many integrations will need additional categories."},{type:"table",headers:["Frequency","Things to do","Purpose"],rows:[["Continuously","Monitor whether the website is accessible or not, and warn as soon as the website stops working","Detect problems before customers"],["Daily or weekly","Automatically back up source code and databases, save copies in a separate server location","There is always a way back when data is lost"],["Every week","Submit a test form, test the call button, WhatsApp, shopping cart; Quickly view error logs","Make sure customers can contact and make purchases"],["Every month","Update plugins, libraries, security patches after testing on the copy","Close loopholes, stay compatible"],["Every month","Check speed, Core Web Vitals, index errors on Google Search Console","Keep experience and rankings"],["Every month","Update content, products, images; Access, contact, order reports","Information is always correct, know how the website is working"],["Every quarter","Try restoring from backup; Check the admin account and access rights","Make sure the copy works, reducing internal risks"],["Every year","Renew domain names, hosting, certificates; Reassess structure, content and goals","Don't lose assets because you forgot to renew, your website keeps up with your business"]]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Don't forget to try recovery",text:"A backup that has never been restored cannot be considered a backup. You should try restoring once every quarter to a separate environment to make sure the data is complete and usable."},{type:"h2",text:"Content maintenance: the most neglected part"},{type:"p",text:"The technical part can be partially automated, but the content needs someone who understands the business. Every month you should review:"},{type:"ul",items:["Is the contact information, business hours, address, and map still correct?","What services, products, and policies have changed but the website has not been updated.","Any new projects, images, or certifications can be added as evidence.","Old articles with outdated data, regulations or timelines need to be edited.","Any internal or external link that is broken will return a 404 error."]},{type:"p",text:"If you want to update content yourself, make sure you have an admin account and documentation. Things like editing the interface, adding features or upgrading the software version should be left to professionals to do on the trial version before posting it on the real website."},{type:"h2",text:"Maintain it yourself, outsource it or give it to the unit that created the website?"},{type:"table",headers:["Plan","suitable when","Risks to note"],rows:[["Do it yourself internally","There are technical personnel and a simple website","Dependent on one person, easy to give up when busy with main tasks"],["Rent another unit","The old unit is no longer supported","Needs time to get familiar with the source code, must have enough accounts and handover documents"],["Assigned to the unit that built the website","Want one focal point to be responsible from start to finish","It is necessary to clearly agree on the tasks, frequency and form of reporting"]]},{type:"p",text:"Regardless of which option you choose, the prerequisite is that the business **retains full ownership rights**: source code, domain name, hosting, administrative account and data. With all of those things, you can always change operators without having to start over."},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"Xartisan Studio Basic operating package",text:"The Basic package is designed to properly preserve assets: manage hosting, domain names, SSL certificates; Periodically backup and monitor website activity; Update content, images, product information; Monthly reports on visits, contacts, orders."},{type:"p",text:"A website is an asset, and every asset needs to be preserved to avoid losing value. A regular maintenance schedule is much easier than troubleshooting or redoing your website after a few years of neglect. See [monthly operating model](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website), read more about [website security](/blog/bao-mat-website-ssl-sao-luu-cap-nhat), or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) to discuss the current status of your website."}],faq:[{question:"How often does website maintenance occur?",answer:"Some things happen continuously, such as monitoring website activity and automatic backups; Some do monthly such as software updates, speed checks, reports; Some do it quarterly or annually like trying to restore data or renew domain names. You should not wait for the website to fail before maintaining it."},{question:"Does a website with little content change need maintenance?",answer:"Still needed. Even when content stands still, software, libraries, SSL certificates, and server environments change. Websites that have not been updated for a long time can easily generate errors and be vulnerable to attacks."},{question:"How is warranty and maintenance different?",answer:"Warranty is the web company's commitment to what has been handed over. Maintenance is a periodic job so that the website does not degrade. At Xartisan Studio, the warranty includes free correction within the accepted scope for 5 years (60 months) and a lifetime warranty against errors caused by Xartisan Studio; New features or changes beyond the scope of the cost are quoted in advance."},{question:"Can businesses maintain their website themselves?",answer:"Okay for things like updating content, sending test forms, viewing reports, if you have an admin account and documentation. Software updates, technical error handling and data recovery should be performed by a qualified person on a previous trial."},{question:"What do you need to prepare if you want to change the website operator?",answer:"Need enough source code, domain account, hosting, website administration, measurement tools and handover documents. When the business has all these accounts in its name, the transfer takes place quickly and there is no need to redo the website."}]},{slug:"do-luong-website-ga4-search-console",title:"Measuring websites with GA4 and Search Console: what do business owners need to see each month?",metaTitle:"GA4 and Search Console: what business owners need to see each month | Xartisan Studio",description:"Guide business owners to read website data every month: properly install GA4, Search Console and conversion events, 8 numbers to watch and how to turn data into things to do.",keywords:["ga4","google search console","website measurement","measure conversions","Monthly website reports"],category:"SEO & optimization",tags:["GA4","Search Console","Measurement"],date:"2026-09-19",updated:"2026-09-22",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"No need to become an analytics expert, business owners just need to answer a few questions correctly each month: where do customers come from, what do they see, and are they in contact? Here's how to install and read data correctly.",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi","website-chuan-seo-la-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many websites have Google Analytics installed but the business owner has never opened it, or opened it and saw too many numbers and closed it. Measurement is not about creating pretty reports. Its purpose is to answer a few very specific business questions: **where do visitors come from, what do they look at, and how many actually reach out or buy**. This article will help you set it up correctly from the beginning and know where to look each month."},{type:"h2",text:"Two free tools, two different roles"},{type:"table",headers:["Criteria","Google Analytics 4 (GA4)","Google Search Console"],rows:[["Answer the question","What do customers do on the website?","How does the website appear on Google?"],["Key data","Users, traffic sources, page views, events, conversions","Impressions, clicks, search queries, average position, index status"],["Scope","Every channel: Google, advertising, social networks, direct access","Only natural Google search results"],["Detect the problem","The form is not recorded, the page has an abnormal churn rate","Page not indexed, Core Web Vitals error, security issue"]]},{type:"p",text:"The two tools complement each other: Search Console shows whether a website is found and displayed by Google, and GA4 shows whether that visit turned into a customer or not. Without one of them, you only see half the picture."},{type:"h2",text:"Install correctly from the start: 6 things not to miss"},{type:"ol",items:["**Verify Search Console by domain name** (Domain attribute type) to gather enough data for both www and non-www, http and https versions.","**Submit sitemap.xml** in Search Console to let Google know the list of pages to crawl.","**Set up the main event (key event) in GA4** for the correct valuable action: submit form, click call, click WhatsApp, successful order. This is the most important number, more important than visits.","**Link GA4 to Search Console** to see search queries and website behavior in one place.","**Increased GA4 data retention period to 14 months**: default is only 2 months for discovery reports, too short to compare with the same period last year.","**Attach UTM parameters to ad links, messages, emails** to know exactly which campaigns bring in customers."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Visits are not the goal",text:"A website whose visits double but the number of contacts remains the same means the website is not doing its job well. Take **contacts and orders** as the main metrics, visits are just an accompanying metric."},{type:"h2",text:"8 numbers business owners should see every month"},{type:"table",headers:["Business question","See where","Index"],rows:[["How many visitors does the website bring?","GA4, main event","Form numbers, calls, WhatsApp messages, orders"],["Which channel do visitors come from?","GA4, traffic source report","Key visits and events by channel: organic search, advertising, social, direct"],["Which pages are doing well?","GA4, landing page report","Key events for each landing page"],["Does Google see more websites?","Search Console, performance reports","Impressions and clicks compared to last month, same period"],["What keywords do customers search for on the website?","Search Console, query","New queries appear, queries get a lot of impressions but few clicks"],["Have any important pages dropped from Google?","Search Console, indexing reports","The page is not indexed and why"],["Is the website fast enough?","Search Console, Core Web Vitals report","Number of URLs that are Poor or Need Improvement"],["Is the website stable?","Uptime tracking tool","Number of outages and recovery time"]]},{type:"p",text:"These eight numbers are enough to answer the biggest question: is the website working for the business? Don't judge by a single month's figures; Compare it with the previous month and the same period last year to avoid confusion due to seasonality, holidays or a short-term campaign."},{type:"h2",text:"How to read data to make decisions?"},{type:"p",text:"Data is only valuable when it leads to something to be done. Some common situations:"},{type:"ul",items:["**More impressions but few clicks**: title and description on Google are not attractive or do not match search intent. Rewrite the title and meta description for those pages.","**Many visits but few contacts**: landing page lacks evidence, contact button is hard to see on the phone or form is too long. Prioritize conversion optimization before attracting more visits.","**A new query appears regularly**: customers are looking for a need that the website does not yet have its own page. Consider writing an article or creating a new service page.","**Important pages are not indexed**: check for technical errors, duplicate content or pages that are too thin. This is something that needs to be handled immediately.","**Main event suddenly returned to 0**: most likely the form or measurement code was corrupted, not the customer disappeared. Submit the form to test."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Record any changes",text:"Every time you edit your website, run a campaign or change your sales policy, record the date and content of the change. When data fluctuates, you will know the cause instead of having to guess."},{type:"h2",text:"Measurement errors cause data to be misleading"},{type:"ul",items:["Installing the GA4 code twice, causing views and events to be counted twice.","Not excluding internal access, employees visit the website every day, causing the data to swell.","Set key events for actions that have no business value, like scrolling or viewing any page.","Change the domain name or redo the website but forget to switch the measurement code and Search Console configuration.","No UTM attached, so visits from text messages, emails or QR codes are combined with direct visits."]},{type:"h2",text:"What should the monthly report contain?"},{type:"p",text:"A report for a business owner should be short, read in a few minutes and always have three parts: **results** (contacts, orders, customer sources), **website health** (speed, index, problems, backups) and **what to do next month**. In Xartisan Studio's model, the Setup Package includes GA4 measurement, Search Console and conversion events; Monthly operational packages have reports using real data from measurement tools, especially the Performance package has weekly reports."},{type:"p",text:"Measurement turns your website from an unpredictable expense into an asset where you know how it's doing. If the current website does not have reliable data, please see [scope of SEO and measurement](/dich-vu-seo-website), re-read [12 standard SEO website criteria](/blog/website-chuan-seo-la-gi), include data review in [monthly maintenance schedule](/blog/bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi), or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) to check the structure measurement form."}],faq:[{question:"Are there any fees for GA4 and Search Console?",answer:"Are not. Both are free tools from Google. The cost lies in getting the installation time right, setting up conversion events, and reading metrics periodically."},{question:"How long does it take for a new website to have data on Search Console?",answer:"Once verified, data usually starts appearing within a few days. However, a new website needs more time for Google to crawl, index and display for many queries."},{question:"Which index should be the main target?",answer:"The number of contacts or orders that the website brings in, measured by key events in GA4. Visits, viewing time or rankings are just supporting indicators."},{question:"Why is the number of orders in GA4 different from the actual number of orders?",answer:"GA4 may be missing data when users decline cookies, use ad blockers, or when measurement code is corrupted. You should compare GA4 with actual order and contact data and use GA4 to see trends and customer sources."},{question:"How long does Search Console save data?",answer:"Search Console performance reports show approximately the last 16 months of data. If you want a longer comparison, you should export data periodically every month."}]},{slug:"bao-mat-website-ssl-sao-luu-cap-nhat",title:"Website security: SSL, backups, updates and risks of neglect",metaTitle:"Website security for businesses: SSL, backup, updates | Xartisan Studio",description:"Three basic layers of protection for a business website: SSL certificate, proper backups, and regular updates. Risk of forgetting, security checklist and 6 steps to handle when your website is attacked.",keywords:["website security","ssl certificate","website backup","website was hacked","update website"],category:"Operations & security",tags:["Security","SSL","Backup"],date:"2026-09-12",updated:"2026-09-15",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"A website doesn't need to be a big target to be attacked. The tool automatically scans a series of websites to find loopholes: expired SSL, old software, weak passwords. Here's what to do to avoid becoming an easy target.",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi","ten-mien-va-hosting-cho-doanh-nghiep"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many business owners think their website is small and has nothing to lose, so no one will attack it. In fact, most website attacks do not target a specific business. They are performed by an automated mass scanning tool to find websites with outdated software, weak passwords, or misconfigurations. A hijacked website can have gambling ads inserted, used to distribute malware, send spam, or have data wiped out. The good news is that three basic layers of protection significantly reduce risk: **SSL, backups, and updates**."},{type:"h2",text:"Layer 1: SSL and HTTPS certificates"},{type:"p",text:"SSL encrypts data exchanged between the browser and website, so that customer information entered in the form, password or shipping address cannot be read on the transmission line. Website with SSL running using **https** protocol; A website without or with an expired certificate will be warned by the browser that it is not secure, and very few visitors will continue after that warning."},{type:"ul",items:["Use a valid certificate for both the main domain and the www version.","Turn on **automatic renewal**. The maximum validity of SSL certificates is being gradually shortened by the industry, and manual renewal is easy to forget.","Redirect all http to https, avoid the situation where the page sometimes has and sometimes does not have a security key.","Check for mixed content: images, scripts loaded via http on https pages cause the browser to lower the trust level."]},{type:"p",text:"Free certificates like Let's Encrypt are secure enough for most business websites. What matters is not the type of certificate, but that it is **always valid**."},{type:"h2",text:"Layer 2: Back up properly, not just have backups"},{type:"p",text:"Backups are the final layer of protection: when everything else fails, they are the only thing that will help you get your website back. But many websites \"have backups\" but cannot be used when needed, because the copy is located on the same server that has been attacked, lacks a database, or is many months old."},{type:"ul",items:["**Back up full source code, databases and uploaded files** like images, documents, not just parts.","**Apply the 3-2-1 rule**: at least 3 copies, on 2 different storage types, 1 copy placed in a separate location from the main server.","**Frequency according to level of change**: sales website with orders every day needs to be backed up at least daily; The website introduces few changes and may be more sparse.","**Keep multiple versions**: sometimes malicious code lies dormant for several weeks before being discovered, requiring a copy before that time.","**Try restoring periodically** to make sure the copy is available when needed."]},{type:"h2",text:"Layer 3: Software updates and account management"},{type:"p",text:"Each website runs on many layers of software: server operating system, programming language, source code, libraries, themes, plugins. Vulnerabilities are discovered and published continuously; When a patch is available but the website is not updated, automated attack tools will come. For websites using WordPress, most of the announced vulnerabilities lie in plugins and themes, so the more unnecessary plugins you install, the higher the risk."},{type:"ul",items:["Update security patches early, but try on a copy first to avoid interface errors.","Remove plugins, themes, accounts that are no longer in use. Do not use jailbreak themes or plugins, which are often pre-installed with malicious code.","Long, separate admin password, enable **two-factor authentication** for website, hosting, domain and email admin accounts.","Each person has an account, with the necessary permissions. Revoke rights immediately when the employee quits or changes support units.","Protect forms with anti-spam mechanisms and check input data."]},{type:"h2",text:"Risk of neglect: summary table"},{type:"table",headers:["Forgotten category","It's possible","Impact on business"],rows:[["SSL expires","Browser blocks with unsafe warning","Customers leave immediately, advertising money pays for useless clicks"],["There are no usable backups","Data loss when the server fails or is attacked","Had to redo website, lost orders and customer history"],["Software not updating","Inserted malicious code, gambling links, scam pages","Google warns or lowers the display, brand reputation is affected"],["Loose account","Ex-users or crooks access the admin page","Content was edited, customer data was exposed"],["Domain name and hosting forgot to renew","Website stops working, domain name may be registered by someone else","Lost address that has been built for many years"]]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Customer data is the responsibility of the business",text:"Contact forms, orders, member accounts all contain personal data. Exposing data not only loses credibility but can also violate regulations on personal data protection. Only collect information that is truly needed and limit who can see it."},{type:"h2",text:"Website is attacked: 6 steps to handle"},{type:"ol",items:["**Record current situation**: take screenshots, record unusual times and phenomena.","**Change password now** website administration, hosting, database, domain names and related emails.","**Isolate website** if necessary: ​​temporarily return to the maintenance page to avoid spreading malicious code to visitors.","**Restore from a clean backup** before the infection, then patch the exploited vulnerability. Restoring without patching will sooner or later cause the problem again.","**Check Search Console**, security issues section; Once processed, submit a review request to remove the warning.","**Learning from experience**: identify the root cause and add the missing layer of protection."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Self-test in 2 minutes",text:"Type a website address starting with http and see if it automatically switches to https; Click on the icon to the left of the address bar to see how long the certificate is valid for; Ask the person in charge what date the last backup was and where it is saved."},{type:"p",text:"Security is not a one-time job at handover, but a **protection** part of preserving a digital asset. In Xartisan Studio's operating model, the Basic package includes hosting management, domain name, SSL certificate, periodic backups and website monitoring. See [monthly operating packages](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website), [warranty and handover policy](/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website), [website maintenance checklist](/blog/bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi), or [contact](/lien-he) to discuss the current status of your website."}],faq:[{question:"Do small websites need to worry about security?",answer:"Have. Most attacks are carried out automatically on a large scale, regardless of whether the website is large or small. Websites with old software, weak passwords, or no SSL are all vulnerable to exploitation."},{question:"Are free SSL certificates safe?",answer:"Regarding encryption, free certificates like Let's Encrypt are secure enough for most business websites. The thing to pay attention to is configuring automatic renewal so the certificate never expires."},{question:"Hosting already has backups, do I need to have separate backups?",answer:"There should be. The hosting provider's copy is often located on the same infrastructure, which may limit the number of days of storage or charge a fee for restoration. An independent copy controlled by the enterprise is an important layer of security."},{question:"How often should a website be updated?",answer:"Critical security patches should be applied as soon as possible. Regular updates can be done monthly, always test on a copy before posting to the real website."},{question:"Who is responsible for security errors due to the website developer's code?",answer:"Depending on the contract and warranty policy of each unit. With Xartisan Studio, errors caused by Xartisan Studio are covered by a lifetime warranty, in addition to a commitment to free correction within the accepted scope for 5 years (60 months)."}]},{slug:"checklist-landing-page-chay-quang-cao",title:"Checklist landing page before running ads: 20 points to check",metaTitle:"Checklist landing page before running ads 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"20 points to check on your landing page before turning on ads: message, mobile experience, speed, conversion measurement, UTM and post-contact customer care process.",keywords:["checklist landing page","Landing page runs ads","Optimize landing pages","Measure ad conversions"],category:"SEO & optimization",tags:["Landing page","Advertisement","Convert"],date:"2026-09-05",updated:"2026-09-05",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"Advertising money starts running from the first click. A small error like an unsendable form or incorrect measurement code can burn your budget for days without anyone knowing. Check these 20 points before turning on your campaign.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-landing-page",related:["landing-page-la-gi","do-luong-website-ga4-search-console"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"When ads are enabled, each click costs money. If the landing page loads slowly, the message misaligns with the ad, or the form fails to send, budget continues to flow without bringing in any customers. Worse, if the measurement code is wrong, you won't know where your campaign is losing money. The checklist below collects **20 points to check before running ads**, divided into four groups. If you are not sure what a landing page is, you can read the article [what is a landing page and when should you use it](/blog/landing-page-la-gi) first."},{type:"h2",text:"Group 1: Message and content"},{type:"ol",items:["**Match the message**: the landing page title repeats the exact promise in the ad. Customers who click for offer A must see offer A on the first screen.","**One single goal**: the whole page leads to one main action, like leaving a phone number, sending a WhatsApp message or placing an order.","**Benefits first, features later**: clearly state what the customer gets, what problem it solves, then the parameters.","**Real evidence**: actual photos, completed projects, certification, clear return or warranty policy.","**Answer concerns in advance**: delivery or deployment time, costs incurred, payment methods, who will contact you."]},{type:"h2",text:"Group 2: Experience on the phone and speed"},{type:"ol",items:["**Check on real phone**, using mobile network, not just office wifi. For most industries, the majority of ad clicks come from phones.","**Fast loading first screen**: compressed images, no heavy auto-play videos. Google recommends that the main content (LCP) be displayed within 2.5 seconds.","**Call-to-action buttons are always visible**, clickable with one finger, and repeat after important content sections.","**Short form**: only asks what is needed to contact you again, usually name and phone number. Each extra cell reduces the number of senders.","**Call and WhatsApp buttons work properly**: press test to make sure the phone number and WhatsApp link do not have any wrong characters."]},{type:"h2",text:"Group 3: Conversion measurement"},{type:"ol",items:["**Main event in GA4** for correct action: successfully submit form, click call, click WhatsApp, place order.","**Advertising platform conversion tags** such as Google Ads, Meta Pixel, TikTok Pixel are installed and events are recorded correctly, without double counting.","**Attach UTM to each ad**: source, channel, campaign name, to compare effectiveness between ad groups.","**Thank you page or success notification** after submitting the form, both confirms to the customer and is a reliable conversion measurement point.","**Try a real conversion** and check it shows up in GA4 as well as in ads manager."]},{type:"p",text:"How to set up main events and read post-campaign metrics is detailed in the article [measuring websites with GA4 and Search Console](/blog/do-luong-website-ga4-search-console)."},{type:"h2",text:"Group 4: Legal, policies and procedures for handling guests"},{type:"ol",items:["**Clear business information**: company name, address, phone number, and privacy policy when collecting customer data.","**Content complies with advertising policy**: no over-commitments, no misleading images or promises; Industries such as healthcare, pharmaceuticals, and finance often have their own regulations.","**Notify immediately when there is a new customer**: email, text message or CRM notifies the person in charge, do not let the contact lie dormant in the mailbox.","**Regulate response time**: who calls back, how long, what to say. Slow callbacks can lose customers even if the ad and landing page are good.","**Monitoring plan for the first days**: who sees the data, what threshold to stop or adjust the campaign."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"The most expensive mistake is the one no one sees",text:"The form reports being sent successfully but the email is not returned, or the contact goes into an unreadable mailbox, which is a very common error. Please try sending the form with a real phone number and check if the person in charge receives the notification."},{type:"h2",text:"Quick check sheet 15 minutes before advertising time"},{type:"table",headers:["Check","How to do it","Dat when"],rows:[["Advertising link","Try clicking each ad in preview mode","Open the correct landing page, have UTM, no 404 error"],["Form","Test sending with real information","The customer sees a success notification and the person in charge receives the contact"],["Call and WhatsApp","Click try on the phone","Call the correct number, open the correct WhatsApp account"],["Measurement","See GA4's real-time reporting and the ad platform's tag testing tool","The event is recorded once, with the correct name"],["Speed","Run PageSpeed Insights for mobile","There are no serious warnings about images or scripts"],["Content","Reread the title, price, offer, deadline","Exactly matches the ad"]]},{type:"h2",text:"After turning on: monitor and optimize in the first 7 days"},{type:"p",text:"The first days are not to conclude whether the campaign will win or lose, but to detect errors and signals early. Take a look every day: clicks, conversions, cost per contact, and actual contact quality. If there are many clicks without conversions, retest the landing page before increasing the budget. If you make a lot of contacts but can't close, the problem may lie in your targeting or callback process."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Try only one change at a time",text:"When optimizing, change only one element at a time, such as a title, image or form, to see exactly which changes make a difference."},{type:"p",text:"The landing page is a campaign asset: carefully prepared, it helps each advertising dollar work more effectively and can be reused for future sales seasons. In the Growth operating package, Xartisan Studio creates landing pages for the campaign and sales season as part of asset development. See [landing page design scope](/thiet-ke-landing-page), or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) to review the checklist before running."}],faq:[{question:"Should I run ads on the homepage instead of the landing page?",answer:"With campaigns for a specific product, service or offer, a landing page is often more effective because the message is focused and there is only one main action. The homepage is more suitable for brand advertising."},{question:"How many fields should a landing page form have?",answer:"Less is more, usually just a name and phone number. Only add fields when the information is truly needed to advise or classify customers."},{question:"What measurement codes need to be installed?",answer:"At least GA4 with the main event and conversion tag of the advertising platform in use, such as Google Ads, Meta Pixel or TikTok Pixel. All should be tested with a test conversion before running."},{question:"How long does it take to evaluate the effectiveness of a landing page?",answer:"Sufficient data is needed, usually after a few dozen to a few hundred clicks depending on the industry and product price. The first days are mainly to detect errors and signals early, do not rush to conclusions."},{question:"Can one landing page be used for multiple campaigns?",answer:"Yes if the campaigns have the same product and message. When offers or audiences are different, there should be separate versions so the message matches each ad."}]},{slug:"khi-nao-nen-lam-lai-website",title:"When should you redo your website? 8 signs and how to do it again without losing rankings",metaTitle:"When should you redo your website? 8 signs to recognize | Xartisan Studio",description:"8 signs that your website is time for a remake, how to decide between upgrading and refreshing, and a conversion checklist to help keep your Google rankings and data when changing your website.",keywords:["redo the website","website redesign","website upgrade","Convert your website without losing SEO"],category:"Experience in choosing services",tags:["Rework the website","Upgrade","SEO"],date:"2026-08-29",updated:"2026-09-02",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"Not every old website needs to be redone and redone, but there are times when patchwork repairs just cost more money. The 8 signs below help you decide, along with how to do it again without losing your Google rankings.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website",related:["website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi","toi-uu-toc-do-website-core-web-vitals"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A website has a lifespan, but that lifespan is not measured in years but by whether it still does its job well or not. There are many years old websites that still bring in customers regularly because they are well taken care of; There are websites that are only two years old and are outdated because they were built on the wrong foundation or were neglected. This article gives **8 specific signs** for you to evaluate for yourself, how to decide between upgrading and redoing, and what you must do to not lose your Google rankings when moving to a new website."},{type:"h2",text:"8 signs that your website needs to be redone"},{type:"ol",items:["**Poor display on phone**: small text, buttons close together, have to zoom in to read. When most guests watch on their phones, this is the most serious sign.","**Slow loading despite optimization**: images have been compressed, hosting has been upgraded but the website is still sluggish, often due to old platforms or overlapping source code over many years of patching.","**Cannot update yourself**: if you want to edit a line of text, you have to ask an old person, or no one will know what the website is written in.","**No ownership**: domain name, hosting or source code is in someone else's name, the business does not have a full administrator account.","**Outdated platform, not updatable**: software version has been discontinued, plugins abandoned, updating one thing breaks another.","**Images and messages no longer match the business**: the brand has changed, services have expanded, but the website still tells the story of many years ago.","**Not bringing in customers**: there is traffic but no contact, or no one knows how many customers the website brings because there is no measurement.","**Not expandable**: want to add service pages, online sales, multilingual or CRM connection but the current structure does not allow it."]},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"One or two signs does not necessarily mean it needs to be done again",text:"If your website is experiencing only mild symptoms such as being a bit slow or having outdated content, an upgrade may be enough. When encountering three or more signs, especially loss of ownership or the platform not being updated, redoing is often more economical than patching."},{type:"h2",text:"Upgrade or remake: decision table"},{type:"table",headers:["Status","Should upgrade when","Should do it again when"],rows:[["Platform","Still supported and updated normally","Support has been discontinued, cannot be updated"],["Source code","Clearly, there are documents, there are people who understand","Overlapping, no one knows, no documents"],["Ownership","The business has its full name","Missing source code or important accounts"],["Theme","Some parts need to be refreshed, the layout is still fine","Doesn't respond to phone calls, completely off brand"],["Business goals","Keep it the same, just optimize","Big changes: more sales, market expansion"]]},{type:"p",text:"Upgrading is appropriate when the foundation is in good condition and only a few parts need to be renewed. Rework is appropriate when the foundation itself is the problem: the platform is no longer supported, the source code is unknown, or the business doesn't own the core components. Fixing on a broken foundation is like repainting a cracked wall."},{type:"h2",text:"Rebuild your website without losing Google rankings"},{type:"p",text:"The biggest risk when redoing a website lies not in the interface but in **SEO**. Pages that are receiving rankings and visits from Google are assets accumulated over many years; If you change the link without redirecting, Google considers it a new page and rankings may drop sharply. Required Checklist:"},{type:"ol",items:["**Make a list of all old URLs**, especially pages with visits and external links, based on Search Console and GA4 data.","**Keep the same URL** of important pages if possible; If you have to change, create a table mapping each old URL to the corresponding new URL.","**Set 301 redirects** for each old URL to the new page that is closest in meaning, not all to the home page.","**Keep or improve the content** of pages that are currently ranking, do not cut down the content that is bringing in visitors.","**Transfer full title, meta description, structured data and measurement code** to the new website.","**Submit new sitemap and monitor Search Console** for a few weeks after launch, immediately handle 404 errors and unindexed pages."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Don't shut down your old website before the new website is ready",text:"Build a new website on a test environment, test it carefully before transferring the domain name. Periods of time when your website is inaccessible or redirected incorrectly can lose visitors and affect rankings."},{type:"h2",text:"What to prepare before redoing the website?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Recover full ownership rights**: domain name account, hosting, website administration, Search Console, GA4 from the old unit.","**Take current data as a benchmark**: number of visits, number of contacts, pages bringing in the most visitors.","**Note what's working** to keep, and what customers complain about to fix.","**Define new goals**: which customer groups the website needs to bring in, through what actions, and what metrics to measure.","**Prepare updated content and images**: new project, team, certification, policies."]},{type:"p",text:"This is also a good opportunity to review the page structure: which pages are redundant, which pages are missing, which services need separate pages. You can refer to the suggestions in the article [what pages are needed for a business website](/blog/website-business-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi). If the main reason is that the website is slow, carefully measure it first according to the instructions [optimize speed and Core Web Vitals](/blog/toi-uu-toc-do-website-core-web-vitals), because sometimes optimizing in the right place is enough."},{type:"h2",text:"Do it again, keep it every month"},{type:"p",text:"Many websites have to be redone not because the initial design is bad, but because after handover no one takes care of it: the software is not updated, the content is not added, errors accumulate over the years. So when redoing, consider how the website will operate afterward. With Xartisan Studio, the new website is built in the Setup Package with foundational technical SEO, measurement from day one and handover of 100% of source code, domain name, data, and administrative account; Businesses can then choose a monthly operating package to keep assets from deteriorating."},{type:"p",text:"If your current website has three or more of these signs, it's time for a serious evaluation. Refer to [custom website design service](/thiet-ke-website), [workflow from request to handover](/quy-trinh-thiet-ke-website), or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) for advice on whether to upgrade or redo."}],faq:[{question:"How often should you redo your website?",answer:"There is no fixed landmark. A well-run website can last for many years and only requires partial upgrades. You should do it again when you encounter many signs such as an outdated platform, poor display on the phone, or no longer suitable for business goals."},{question:"Will redoing a website lose Google rankings?",answer:"It's possible, if you change the URL without a 301 redirect, truncate the content or forget to move the SEO tags. When the conversion process is done correctly, risks are significantly reduced and the new website has a better foundation to improve future rankings."},{question:"Should I keep the old domain name when redoing my website?",answer:"Should keep. Old domains carry with them history and accumulated trust with Google and customers. The condition is that the business holds the right to manage that domain name."},{question:"What if the old website was made by another unit without source code?",answer:"You can still do it again on the old domain name if the business can manage the domain name. Content can be retrieved from the running website. If the domain name is in the name of the old unit, you need to request a transfer of rights first."},{question:"How long does it take to redo a website?",answer:"Depending on the number of pages, features and content availability. Progress is finalized after analyzing requirements, with time for testing and conversion steps to not affect rankings."}]},{slug:"seo-local-google-business-profile",title:"What is local SEO? Optimize Google Business Profile for local businesses",metaTitle:"Local SEO and Google Business Profile for businesses 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"Local SEO instructions for businesses with stores, offices or service areas: set up Google Business Profile, manage reviews, synchronize information and optimize the website according to locality.",keywords:["seo local","google business profile","google maps business","local seo","Optimize Google Maps"],category:"SEO & optimization",tags:["SEO local","Google Maps","Google Business Profile"],date:"2026-08-22",updated:"2026-08-25",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"When visitors search with recent words or district or city names, Google prioritizes displaying maps and business profiles. This is a way for local businesses to appear right when customers need them.",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["website-chuan-seo-la-gi","viet-noi-dung-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A car repair shop, a clinic, a furniture showroom or a service company in a province all have one common characteristic: customers find them by **location**. Queries like “air conditioner repair district 7,” “dentist nearby” or “printing factory Quy Nhon” often display a map with a few prominent businesses at the top of the results. Being visible in that group is the goal of **local SEO**, and the central tool is Google Business Profile, formerly known as Google My Business."},{type:"h2",text:"What is local SEO and how does it work?"},{type:"p",text:"Local SEO is optimal for businesses to appear in location-based search results, including map blocks on Google Search and results on Google Maps. According to Google's documentation, local results are primarily based on three factors:"},{type:"table",headers:["Factor","Meaning","What impact can businesses have?"],rows:[["Relevance level","Where does the profile match the needs of the person looking for it?","Categories, services, descriptions, website content"],["Distance","How far is the business from the searcher's location?","Almost nothing, other than declaring the correct address or service area"],["Outstanding level","How is the business known and evaluated?","Reviews, images, website content, presence on other sites"]]},{type:"p",text:"Google also makes it clear that there is no way to pay or request to rank higher in organic local results. Advertising is a separate area and is always labeled sponsored."},{type:"h2",text:"Set up your Google Business Profile correctly from the start"},{type:"ol",items:["**Business name is correct** on signs and documents. Do not insert additional keywords or place names into the name; This violates Google's guidelines and may result in your profile being suspended.","**Choose the most accurate primary category**, then add subcategories for related services. The category strongly influences which records appear for which queries.","**Address or service area**: If there is a store that welcomes customers, declare the address; If you come to serve customers in person, set up a service area and you can hide the address.","**Phone number, opening hours, website** accurate, updated including holiday hours.","**Descriptions, services and products** are written clearly and naturally, saying exactly what customers need to know.","**Real images**: facade, interior, team, products, construction. Real photos help guests recognize the location and gain more trust.","**Complete verification** according to Google's instructions so that your profile is fully visible and your business has full control."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Don't use fake addresses or create duplicate profiles",text:"Google requires businesses to have a physical location or actually serve customers in the declared area. Virtual offices, borrowed addresses, or multiple listings for the same location may result in listings being removed, taking all accumulated reviews with them."},{type:"h2",text:"Customer reviews: the profile's most valuable asset"},{type:"p",text:"Ratings influence both salience and viewer decisions. A profile with many real reviews, thoughtful feedback from the business owner, is much more trustworthy than a profile that is empty or full of general compliments."},{type:"ul",items:["**Proactively ask for reviews** after each good service: send review link via WhatsApp, print QR code at the counter, gently remind when handing over the product or project.","**Respond to all reviews**, even negative reviews. Respond calmly, accept responsibility if any and provide specific solutions.","**Do not buy reviews, do not exchange gifts for reviews**, do not write your own reviews. Google prohibits these practices and may remove reviews or restrict profiles.","**Not selectively inviting people**: only inviting guests who are satisfied and avoiding guests who may criticize is also a practice that Google does not allow."]},{type:"h2",text:"Synchronize information everywhere your business appears"},{type:"p",text:"Name, address and phone number, often abbreviated as NAP, should be the same on Google Business Profile, website, directory pages, social networks and e-commerce platforms. Discrepant information makes it difficult for Google to determine which data is correct, while customers call the wrong number or go to the wrong address. When moving locations or changing phone numbers, make a list of places that need to be updated and fixed all at once."},{type:"h2",text:"How does the website support local SEO?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Full contact page**: address, phone number, business hours, embedded map and directions.","**Separate page for each branch or service area** If there are multiple locations, each page has actual content about that location, do not copy and change names.","**LocalBusiness structured data** helps Google understand the exact name, address, and opening hours of a business.","**Local-related content**: projects done in the area, frequently asked questions from guests there.","**Speed and mobile experience**, because the majority of local searches happen on mobile, often when customers need them right away."]},{type:"p",text:"Your profile on Google is where customers see you, and your website is where customers decide whether to contact you or not. A good profile leading to a slow, lacking information website will waste existing interest. See more [12 standard SEO website criteria](/blog/website-chuan-seo-la-gi) and how to [write website content for customers to trust and contact](/blog/viet-noi-dung-website)."},{type:"h2",text:"Checklist maintains monthly records"},{type:"ul",items:["Update opening hours on holidays and any information changes.","Post new photos, updates on products, offers, and projects.","Respond to new reviews as soon as possible.","View the number of calls, directions, and website visits from your profile to evaluate effectiveness.","Check to see if anyone has suggested editing incorrect profile information."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"View profiles through the eyes of guests",text:"Every month, look for the business name and key services on the phone as a new customer. You will immediately see which information is missing, which photos are old, and which reviews have not been answered."},{type:"p",text:"Local SEO has no shortcuts: accurate information, real reviews, a trustworthy website and regular maintenance are things that add up to long-term advantages. Xartisan Studio does not promise to bring your business to the number one position, because no one can control Google's algorithm, but it can help you build the right foundation. See [scope of SEO website](/dich-vu-seo-website) or [contact](/lien-he) to discuss the area and customer group you want to reach."}],faq:[{question:"Does Google Business Profile cost anything?",answer:"Are not. Creating and managing a business profile on Google is free. Cost, if any, lies in the time spent taking care of records, images and content."},{question:"Can a business without a store do local SEO?",answer:"Okay. Door-to-door service businesses can set up service areas and hide addresses. The important thing is to actually serve guests in the declared area."},{question:"How to handle bad reviews that are not true?",answer:"Please respond politely, presenting the situation briefly. If the review violates Google's policies such as spam, offensive content or is not related to actual experiences, you can report it to Google to consider removing it."},{question:"Should multiple profiles be created to cover multiple areas?",answer:"Shouldn't. Each physical location should only have one profile. Creating profiles for bogus addresses violates Google's guidelines and may result in profiles being removed."},{question:"How long does it take to see local SEO results?",answer:"Basic information and verification can be completed quickly, but prominence takes time to accumulate reviews, images, and content. In a competitive market, it needs to be maintained regularly for many months."}]},{slug:"ban-tren-san-hay-lam-website-rieng",title:"Sell ​​on the floor or create your own sales website? Compare to choose the right channel",metaTitle:"Sell on the floor or create your own sales website? Compare 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"Compare selling on Shopee, Lazada, TikTok Shop with your own sales website: costs, customer data, brand, platform-dependent risks and how to combine the two channels effectively.",keywords:["separate sales website","sales on the floor","Should I make a sales website?","shopee hay website","online sales channel"],category:"Experience in choosing services",tags:["Online sales","E-commerce platform","E-commerce website"],date:"2026-08-14",updated:"2026-08-18",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"The e-commerce platform gives you a ready-made customer base, and your own website gives you the right to own your customers and your brand. The question is not one or the other, but what role each channel should play.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-ban-hang",related:["thiet-ke-website-ban-hang-can-gi","ngan-sach-website-nam-dau"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Shopee, Lazada, TikTok Shop help many sellers reach customers without having to build their own channels. So does a business that sells well on the stock marketplace need its own sales website? On the contrary, if you are just starting out, should you go public or build a website first? The answer depends on the product, profit margin, customer base and branding plan. The article compares the two channels in a practical way so that you can assign the correct role to each channel."},{type:"h2",text:"Selling on the floor: advantages and limitations"},{type:"p",text:"The biggest advantage of the platform is **existing customer flow**: buyers are already there, used to paying and receiving goods, so a new shop can place orders quite quickly. The floor also takes care of most of the infrastructure such as payment, shipping, and complaint handling. In return, businesses accept the following limitations:"},{type:"ul",items:["**Multi-layered fees**: fixed fee, payment fee, service fee, program participation fee. The fee schedule is decided by the floor and may change from time to time.","**Competing by price**: your products are located next to dozens of other shops, customers can easily compare prices and switch to a cheaper shop.","**Limited customer data**: buyers are customers of the marketplace; Actively caring for and reselling them is limited by the platform's policies.","**Depends on algorithms and policies**: a change in display, fees or regulations may cause sales fluctuations that the shop has no control over.","**Faded brand**: customers often remember which platform they bought on rather than remember the store name."]},{type:"h2",text:"Own sales website: advantages and challenges"},{type:"p",text:"A private website is a channel **wholly owned by the enterprise**: domain name, interface, customer data, product presentation and sales policy are all decided by the enterprise."},{type:"ul",items:["**Mastering data**: knowing who the customer is, what they buy, and when they buy it again, thereby taking care of it and proactively reselling it.","**Building a brand**: stories, images, policies are presented in a unique way, without being compared next to each other.","**There is no floor fee on each order**, although there are still payment gateway fees, shipping fees and costs to bring customers to the website.","**Suitable for wholesale, selling to businesses, high-value products**: transactions that require consultation, quotes, and capacity profiles that the floor does not support well."]},{type:"p",text:"The challenge is that the website **doesn't have customers on its own**. You must attract customers through SEO, advertising, content, social networks or old customer files, and must have people to operate: product updates, order processing, technical maintenance, and data tracking."},{type:"h2",text:"Quickly compare two channels"},{type:"table",headers:["Criteria","Sold on the floor","Private website"],rows:[["Initial customers","Available, quick ordering","Must pull it back yourself"],["Cost per order","Laminated flooring fees, subject to change","No floor fees; There are passenger and operating costs"],["Customer data","Restrictions according to floor policy","Fully owned business"],["Brand","Difficult to stand out among many shops","Freedom to build"],["Dependency level","High: algorithm, fees, policies","Low: business owned"],["Most suitable","Popular goods, need quick orders","Private brand, repeat customers, wholesale, high value goods"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Don't have to choose just one: the hybrid model works"},{type:"p",text:"For many businesses, the reasonable way is to **use the platform to get orders and use the website to retain customers**. Some common combinations:"},{type:"ol",items:["**Floor finds new customers, website takes care of old customers**: first order comes from the floor; future purchases, membership incentives, and new products introduced through the website.","**Website is the face of the brand**: story, policies, capacity profile, agent system; Customers searching for the brand name on Google will see the main website.","**Website for wholesalers, agents, businesses**: tiered price list, bulk orders, individual quotes, things the floor cannot do.","**Website welcomes visitors from content and SEO**: articles on instructions, comparisons, and product selection advice bring visitors from Google straight to your channel."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"It's okay to start small",text:"No need for a fully featured sales website on day one. You can start with the main product list, clear policies, place an order or send a quick WhatsApp message, then expand the shopping cart and pay online when customers return."},{type:"h2",text:"When should you invest in your own sales website?"},{type:"ul",items:["Revenue on the floor has stabilized, but fees are increasingly eating into profits.","There are many buyers who want to proactively take care of them.","Sell products that require consultation, high value, or wholesale or sell to businesses.","I'm building my own brand, I want customers to remember the store name, not just the floor.","Want to reduce risk when all sales depend on one platform."]},{type:"p",text:"A legal note: websites with online ordering functions often must notify the Ministry of Industry and Trade according to e-commerce regulations, and also need to have full business information, return policies, shipping and security. You should check current regulations before opening for sale. The list of features and things that need to be prepared is in the article [what is needed to design a sales website](/blog/thiet-ke-website-ban-hang-can-gi), and how to divide the construction and operating budget is in the article [first year website budget](/blog/ngan-sach-website-nam-dau)."},{type:"p",text:"The stall on the floor is like a rented stall in a big market: crowded but the rules of the game are set by the market owner. A private website is a storefront in the business's name, an asset that accumulates value over time. If you are considering adding a separate sales channel, see [sales website design service](/thiet-ke-website-ban-hang) or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) to calculate a suitable plan for your existing products and customer base."}],faq:[{question:"New to business, should I go public or build a website first?",answer:"If you need to place an order quickly for popular goods, the platform helps verify the product at a low initial cost. If you sell products that need advice, high value, or want to build a brand from the beginning, you should have a parallel website for customers to find and trust."},{question:"Can the sales website connect to the floor?",answer:"Depending on platform and scope. Synchronization of products, inventory or orders is possible if the platform provides the appropriate connection. This part needs to be unpacked and confirmed before quoting."},{question:"If I have a website, should I leave the marketplace?",answer:"Not necessarily. Many businesses keep both: a platform to reach new customers, a website to build a brand and take care of old customers. The proportion between the two channels should be adjusted according to actual data."},{question:"Where does a private website get customers from?",answer:"From Google search thanks to SEO, advertising, content on social networks, WhatsApp, email and existing customer files. The website needs to be operated and measured to know which channels bring in orders."},{question:"Do I have to notify the Ministry of Industry and Trade to create a sales website?",answer:"Websites with online ordering functions often must notify the Ministry of Industry and Trade according to e-commerce regulations. You should check current regulations or ask the website maker to prepare enough information."}]},{slug:"toi-uu-toc-do-website-core-web-vitals",title:"Optimizing website speed and Core Web Vitals: a guide for business owners",metaTitle:"Optimize website speed, Core Web Vitals for business owners | Xartisan Studio",description:"What is Core Web Vitals, what do the three indicators LCP, INP, CLS mean, how to self-check website speed for free and common causes of slow websites, with solutions.",keywords:["Optimize website speed","core web vitals","website is slow","pagespeed insights","lcp inp cls"],category:"SEO & optimization",tags:["Speed","Core Web Vitals","Performance"],date:"2026-08-07",updated:"2026-08-10",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"Customers don't wait for a slow website. The article explains Core Web Vitals in easy-to-understand language, how to test yourself in 5 minutes, and what to prioritize to make your website faster.",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["website-chuan-seo-la-gi","khi-nao-nen-lam-lai-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Have you ever clicked on a search result, looked at a white screen for a few seconds and then went back to choose another website? Your customers do the same thing. Speed ​​is the first impression of a website, directly affecting whether customers stay, contact or buy. Google also measures this experience using the **Core Web Vitals** set of metrics. The article explains that set of indicators in the language of business owners, no need to know programming."},{type:"h2",text:"What is Core Web Vitals?"},{type:"p",text:"Core Web Vitals are three metrics Google uses to evaluate actual user experience: whether the main content appears quickly, whether the website responds quickly to operations, and whether the layout jumps around. Google's rating is based on real data from Chrome users, at the 75th percentile: a page is considered passable when at least 75% of visits have a good experience."},{type:"table",headers:["Index","Measure something","Good threshold according to Google","Understand simply"],rows:[["LCP (Largest Contentful Paint)","The time the largest piece of content is visible","Within 2.5 seconds","How long does it take for visitors to see the main content?"],["INP (Interaction to Next Paint)","Delay when customers click, touch, or type keys","200 milliseconds or less","Click the button to respond immediately"],["CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift)","The layout level is distorted when loading","From 0.1 or less","Does the page jump causing customers to click on it by mistake?"]]},{type:"p",text:"INP has replaced the FID index since 2024, because it reflects smoothness throughout the visitor's use of the page, not just the first touch."},{type:"h2",text:"How does speed affect business?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Bounce rate**: every extra second of waiting means an additional group of visitors leave before seeing the product or service.","**Advertising effectiveness**: you pay for each click, but if the page loads slowly, the customer leaves before the page can appear and that money is lost.","**SEO**: page experience is one of many Google ranking signals. Speed ​​does not replace good content, but when two sites are equal in content, a better experience is an advantage.","**Belief**: website is slow, jerky, jumpy layout creates a feeling of unprofessionalism, especially for customers who know the business for the first time."]},{type:"h2",text:"Self-test website speed in 5 minutes"},{type:"ol",items:["Open Google's **PageSpeed Insights**, paste the address of the most important homepage or service page.","See the **actual data from users** section at the top of the report if available. This is the data Google uses for evaluation, more important than the score below.","Choose **mobile** mode, as this is usually where the website is slowest and where the majority of visitors are.","Read the diagnostics section to find out the main cause: images are too heavy, scripts block display, server responds slowly.","Go to **Google Search Console**, Core Web Vitals section, to see which groups of pages are Poor or Need Improvement across the website."]},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"Don't chase after 100 points",text:"Performance scores in PageSpeed Insights are the results of testing in a simulated environment and may fluctuate between runs. The real goal is that real user data reaches a good threshold and customers find the website fast, not a round number."},{type:"h2",text:"Common causes of slow websites"},{type:"table",headers:["Cause","Expression","Solution direction"],rows:[["Photo is too heavy, wrong size","Image appears in patches, high LCP","Compress images, use WebP or AVIF format, correct display size, slow load images at the bottom"],["Hosting is weak or located too far from guests","The screen goes blank for a long time before any content appears","Upgrade hosting, use caching and CDN"],["Too many third-party plugins and scripts","Pressing the button is delayed, INP is high","Remove unnecessary things, chat delays, pixels, widgets that are not needed immediately"],["Slider, video plays automatically at the top of the page","Main content appears slowly","Replace with optimized still images, only download videos when visitors click to watch"],["Fonts, banners, advertising frames inserted late","Jump layout, high CLS","Declare the size for the image and embedded frame; Optimize how to download fonts"],["The source code is cumbersome, the built-in interface is too heavy","Every page is slow even with little content","Optimize the source code or consider remaking it on a cleaner platform"]]},{type:"h2",text:"What can business owners do, what needs technology?"},{type:"p",text:"Some things you can do yourself right away: compress photos before uploading, don't insert heavy videos at the top of the page, limit installing chat utilities, popups or tracking codes when you don't really need them. Things like configuring caching, CDN, optimizing source code, handling display-blocking scripts or upgrading servers should be left to professionals and re-measured after each change."},{type:"p",text:"Speed is also not a one-time job. Every new image, new plugin, new ad code can slow down your website. Therefore, checking speed and Core Web Vitals should be part of the monthly [website maintenance](/blog/bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi) schedule. If the website is slow because the platform is too old, read more [8 signs that you should redo your website](/blog/when-nao-nen-re-reform-website)."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Prioritize pages that bring in visitors",text:"There is no need to optimize every page at the same time. Let's start with the homepage, service pages, best-selling product pages and landing pages that are running ads."},{type:"p",text:"A fast website is a well-kept asset: visitors stay longer, advertising is more effective, and Google has more reason to appreciate it. At Xartisan Studio, mobile loading and display speed are part of the foundational technical SEO in the Setup Package. See [scope of SEO website](/dich-vu-seo-website) or [contact](/lien-he) to see the speed report of the current website."}],faq:[{question:"How many seconds does it take for a website to load?",answer:"According to Google's thresholds, main content (LCP) should be displayed within 2.5 seconds, input latency (INP) should be 200 milliseconds or less, and layout deviation (CLS) should be 0.1 or less, across at least 75% of visits."},{question:"Is a low PageSpeed ​​score penalized by Google?",answer:"There is no concept of penalty for low scores. Google uses actual user data as one of many ranking signals. However, a slow website still loses customers, so it needs to be improved."},{question:"Why is the website fast on computers but slow on phones?",answer:"Phones often have weaker configurations and network connections, so heavy images, lots of scripts and complex effects have a more obvious impact. Always check and optimize for mobile first."},{question:"Does changing hosting make the website faster?",answer:"Maybe, if slow server response is the main cause. But if the website is slow because of heavy images or too many scripts, changing hosting will not solve the problem. You should measure to find the correct cause first."},{question:"Where can I see Core Web Vitals for a new website with little traffic?",answer:"When there is not enough traffic, Google does not have actual data for the website. You can then use the test results in PageSpeed ​​Insights to detect problems and gradually monitor them as traffic increases."}]},{slug:"viet-noi-dung-website",title:"What should the website content be written so that customers can trust and proactively contact you?",metaTitle:"Write website content for customers to trust and contact: guide 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"How to write business website content for customers to trust and contact: start from the customer's question, replace general compliments with specific evidence, structure service pages and calls to action.",keywords:["Write website content","corporate website content","content website","service page content"],category:"Basic knowledge",tags:["Content","Convert","Faith"],date:"2026-07-31",updated:"2026-08-04",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"A beautiful interface helps visitors stay for a few seconds, new content is what makes them pick up the phone and call. This is how to write website content that is specific, has evidence, and leads visitors to take action.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website",related:["website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi","seo-local-google-business-profile"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many business websites have a neat interface but the content is strangely similar: \"top reputation\", \"best quality\", \"professional team\", \"competitive prices\". Customers don't remember anything after reading and have no reason to choose this business over competitors. Website content is not to compliment you, but to **answer the questions customers have in mind** and give them enough evidence to believe. This article shows how to do that."},{type:"h2",text:"Start from the customer's question, not from the company introduction"},{type:"p",text:"Before writing, list the questions customers often ask over the phone, on WhatsApp or when meeting in person. That is the content the website needs. Usually customers want to know:"},{type:"ul",items:["Does the business do exactly what I need, and has it done it for anyone like me?","How do I do it, how long does it take, what do I need to prepare?","How are costs calculated, are there any?","If there is a problem after purchase, who is responsible and how to handle it?","What is the fastest way to contact?"]},{type:"p",text:"A website that clearly answers these five questions stands out more than many websites that only have slogans. Costing is not necessarily a price list; With scope-dependent services, explaining the calculation and influencing factors is already a valuable answer."},{type:"h2",text:"Replace general compliments with specific evidence"},{type:"table",headers:["Write in general","Write specifically, with evidence"],rows:[["Top reputation","Legal entity name, tax code, office address, year of commencement of operation"],["Professional team","Real photos, names, roles and experiences of the people directly working"],["Many customers trust","Specific projects have images, links or descriptions of problems and deliverables"],["Best quality","Verifiable testing procedures, material standards, certifications"],["Dedicated support","Written warranty policy: duration, scope, how to receive requests"],["Competitive prices","Explain what costs include and what factors cause costs to change"]]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Don't make up data, don't borrow compliments",text:"Exaggerated data, self-written reviews, or unsolicited customer logos can be discovered with just one search. Then the business loses the trust that the content wants to build. Only post on the website what can be verified."},{type:"h2",text:"Structure a convincing service page"},{type:"p",text:"Service pages are often the most important pages in terms of conversions. An easy-to-apply structure:"},{type:"ol",items:["**The title clearly states the service and object**: readers know they have come to the right place.","**Issue the customer is having**: describe in the customer's language, not industry jargon.","**How businesses solve it**: scope of work, what customers receive.","**Working process**: steps, expected time, what customers need to prepare.","**Proof**: projects, real photos, certifications, verifiable feedback.","**Costs and commitments**: how to calculate costs, warranty policy, what is not included.","**Frequently Asked Questions**: answer questions in advance that often make customers hesitate.","**Clear call to action**: call, text WhatsApp or leave information, with what the customer receives after contacting."]},{type:"h2",text:"Write for readers on the phone"},{type:"ul",items:["**Short sentences, short paragraphs**: each paragraph has one idea, about two to four sentences.","**Clear subheadings**: visitors can understand the main content just by scanning the titles.","**Lists and tables** for information to compare such as service packages, processes, parameters.","**Actual images with captions** instead of illustrations taken online.","**Contact button placed right after the pitch**, where the visitor has just finished reading, not just at the bottom of the page."]},{type:"h2",text:"Content that is good for customers is also good content for SEO"},{type:"p",text:"Google encourages content that is useful, trustworthy, and written for people, not for keyword stuffing. In its search quality assessment guidelines, Google emphasizes experience, expertise, reputation and trustworthiness, often abbreviated as E-E-A-T. Those factors coincide with the writing style above: specific information, the writer has real experience, and the business is transparent."},{type:"p",text:"AI tools can help with outlining or correcting sentences, but the content posted needs to be checked by someone who understands the profession and supplemented with practical experience. Mass-produced content just to get search results, lacking its own value, may be underestimated by Google. For businesses serving regions, content should also be locally relevant, as suggested in the article [SEO local and Google Business Profile](/blog/seo-local-google-business-profile)."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"A valuable source of content that few people use",text:"Record the questions guests ask over the course of a month and how the team responds. Each good question can be turned into a FAQ section, a paragraph on a service page, or a blog post that answers exactly what customers are looking for."},{type:"p",text:"Content is an asset that appreciates over time: each new project, each question answered, each useful article makes the website more trustworthy. See suggestions [what pages a business website needs](/blog/website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi), refer to [implemented Xartisan Studio project](/du-an), or [contact](/lien-he) if you need a website with a clear content structure from the beginning."}],faq:[{question:"Can businesses write website content themselves?",answer:"Yes, and usually you should participate because the business understands customers and products best. A web developer can help with structure, editing, and search optimization."},{question:"What should the introduction page write?",answer:"There should be legal information, years of operation, field, real team, way of working and commitments of the business. The founding story should be brief and related to the value it brings to customers."},{question:"Should prices be published on the website?",answer:"Depends on business model. Standard products should have clear prices. Scope-based services can explain cost calculations and influencing factors, then quote individually after understanding needs."},{question:"Is content written with AI penalized by Google?",answer:"Google evaluates the quality and usefulness of content, not penalizing it just because of the tool that created it. However, mass-produced content that lacks its own value can be considered spam. The content needs to be checked by someone who understands the profession and supplemented with real experience."},{question:"How often should website content be updated?",answer:"Business information such as services, policies, and contacts need to be updated immediately when changed. Projects, images and articles should be added regularly, for example monthly, to keep the website lively and trustworthy."}]},{slug:"chi-phi-an-khi-lam-website-gia-re",title:"Hidden costs when building a cheap website: 9 common ones and how to avoid them",metaTitle:"Hidden costs when building a cheap website and how to avoid them 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"9 common hidden costs when making a cheap website: domain name in someone else's name, skyrocketing renewal fees, each-time repair fee, not handing over source code, unlocked themes and how to recognize before signing.",keywords:["Hidden costs of making a website","cheap website","cheap website design","cheap website risks"],category:"Costs & quotes",tags:["Hidden costs","Cheap price","Risk"],date:"2026-07-23",updated:"2026-07-27",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"The low price when signing the contract does not necessarily mean the low cost of owning a website. Here are 9 common hidden costs, warning signs, and questions to ask before choosing a cheap plan.",ctaService:"/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","hop-dong-thiet-ke-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"There is nothing wrong with a cheap website if it meets your needs and is transparent about what you get. The problem lies in the items **not mentioned at the time of quote** but gradually appear after handover: unusually high renewal fees, fees for each repair, the domain name is in someone else's name, or the website has to be redone after only a year or two. When added up, the real cost of owning a cheap website can be much higher than the initial figure."},{type:"h2",text:"The price of making a website is different from the cost of owning a website"},{type:"p",text:"The price for making a website is the amount paid at the time of signing the contract. **Cost of ownership** is the total amount of money a business spends during the time of using the website: construction, infrastructure, editing, troubleshooting, lost business opportunities when the website slows or stops working, and redo costs if the foundation does not last long. Comparing options should be based on the cost of ownership over several years, not just on the contracted price."},{type:"h2",text:"9 common hidden costs"},{type:"ol",items:["**Domain and hosting names are in the name of the web company**: when you want to change units, businesses have to pay additional fees or negotiate to get it back, or even lose the domain name.","**Renewal fee is much higher than the first year**: the first year is given away or deeply reduced, from the second year the price of hosting and domain name increases sharply without warning.","**No handover of source code**: website only runs on the website maker's system; Stopping cooperation means losing the website.","**Charge for each edit**: changing a phone number, changing a photo also incurs fees or has to wait for many days.","**Theme, jailbreak plugin**: saves royalties but easily contains malicious code, cannot be updated, high risk of being attacked.","**General, heavy template interface**: website is slow, difficult to optimize SEO, difficult to edit as desired; After a while, you have to do it again.","**No backup, no maintenance**: when something goes wrong, you find out there are no copies, the cost of restoring or redoing is huge.","**Photos, fonts, content violate copyright**: photos taken online or copied content may lead to complaints and forced removal.","**Basic features are considered additional**: contact form, SSL, basic SEO standards are reported as advanced packages after signing."]},{type:"h2",text:"Signs to recognize and questions to ask"},{type:"table",headers:["Signs in quotes","Risk","Questions to ask"],rows:[["Do not write down who owns the domain name or hosting","Loss of control over assets","Whose name is the domain and hosting registered under? Do I have a management account?"],["No mention of source code","The operating unit cannot be changed","Will I be handed over the source code and documentation, and when?"],["Price for first year only","Renewal fee increased unexpectedly","How are renewal costs from the second year calculated?"],["Warranty written in general","There is a fee for any repairs","How long is the warranty, what does it include, is there a fee for minor repairs?"],["The range only records page numbers","Basic features have emerged","What functions does each page include, which parts are not included?"],["Interface according to unknown source model","Copyright, security, speed","Are themes and plugins copyrighted? Who pays the renewal fee?"]]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"One question filters many risks",text:"Ask: If I want to transfer to another unit next year, what can I bring with me? The answer will let you know whether you own a asset or are just renting a website."},{type:"h2",text:"Not all cheap websites are scary"},{type:"p",text:"For simple needs like a short introduction page or a test landing page, a low-cost option can make perfect sense. It's important that **the scope is clearly stated, ownership belongs to the business and recurring payments are stated in advance**. Conversely, a high price quote does not by itself guarantee quality; You need to compare quotes on the same scope of work."},{type:"p",text:"The best way to avoid hidden costs is to have everything written down: scope, ownership, warranties, recurring costs, calculations. See more about how to [separate website design costs](/blog/cost-phi-thiet-ke-website) and the [terms needed in a website design contract](/blog/hop-dong-thiet-ke-website)."},{type:"h2",text:"How does Xartisan Studio eliminate hidden costs?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Separate two parts**: Setup package is a one-time investment; Monthly operations Basic, Growth or Performance are periodic payments, clearly stating the beginning of the work.","**100% ownership**: source code, domain name, data and administrative account in the name of the customer business.","**Two-tier warranty**: free correction within the scope of acceptance for 5 years (60 months), and lifetime warranty against errors caused by Xartisan Studio.","**Increasing transparency**: new features or changes outside the scope are reported at cost before implementation, only implemented when you agree.","**Quote separately, clearly stating each item**, after understanding the goals and current status of the business."]},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"Why doesn't Xartisan Studio publish the price list?",text:"A common number can easily cause you to make false comparisons between very different ranges. Xartisan Studio communicates to understand the goal first, then sends a separate quote with full one-time and recurring costs, no hidden fees."},{type:"p",text:"A website is an asset, and the asset only truly belongs to you when the documents, accounts and expenses are clear. Before choosing the cheapest plan, calculate the cost of ownership over several years. See [warranty and handover policy](/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website) of Xartisan Studio, or [contact](/lien-he) via WhatsApp 0435 878 929 to receive a separate quote clearly stating each item."}],faq:[{question:"Can a cheap website last a long time?",answer:"It is possible, if built on a good foundation, the scope is clear and the business has enough ownership. The risk lies in packages that lack transparency about source code, domain names, warranties and renewal fees."},{question:"How do I know if the domain name is in my business name?",answer:"Ask the web company for information about the registrant and request a domain management account. You can look up WHOIS with international domain names or VNNIC's lookup tool with.vn domain names, although some information may be hidden."},{question:"How dangerous are jailbreak themes and plugins?",answer:"Jailbreaks are often modified and may contain malicious code, not receive security patches, and violate copyrights. Websites using them are susceptible to inserting strange content, redirecting to another page or losing data."},{question:"What if I accidentally made a website without the source code?",answer:"Please ask the old unit to hand over source code, data and transfer domain and hosting rights. If that's not possible, at least you need to regain domain management rights so you can build a new website without losing the addresses you already know."},{question:"Does Xartisan Studio charge a fee to repair the website after handover?",answer:"Corrections within the accepted scope are free for 5 years (60 months), and errors caused by Xartisan Studio are warranted for life. New features or changes outside the scope are quoted at a cost before implementation."}]},{slug:"hop-dong-thiet-ke-website",title:"What terms are needed in a website design contract? Checklist before signing",metaTitle:"Website design contract: necessary terms before signing | Xartisan Studio",description:"Checklist of terms needed in a website design contract: scope of work, progress and acceptance, payment, ownership of source code and domain name, handover, warranty, handling of scope changes.",keywords:["website design contract","website contract terms","web design contract template","website acceptance"],category:"Experience in choosing services",tags:["Contract","Legal","Handover"],date:"2026-07-16",updated:"2026-07-20",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"Many disagreements when making a website do not come from technicalities but from things that are not written down. These are 10 groups of clauses that should be included in the contract to protect both the business and the website maker.",ctaService:"/quy-trinh-thiet-ke-website",related:["chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-uy-tin","chi-phi-an-khi-lam-website-gia-re"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A website usually takes a few weeks to a few months to complete and is associated with a business for many years. During that time, the two sides will have many exchanges: add a page, change a color, fix a feature. If the contract only states a general website design package with a number, every small change can become controversial. A clear contract is not to prevent each other, but so that **both parties have the same understanding** about what will be done and the assets that will be handed over."},{type:"h2",text:"10 groups of terms that should be included in a website design contract"},{type:"table",headers:["Terms","Need to clearly state","Why is it important?"],rows:[["1. Scope of work","List of pages, functions, number of editing rounds, content prepared by which party","Is the basis for acceptance and any future changes"],["2. Progress","Milestones for design approval, programming completion, testing, and launch; Responsibility when late","Avoid projects that last forever"],["3. Payment","Number of installments and value of each installment are tied to work milestones and payment methods","Money comes with results, fair for both sides"],["4. Acceptance","Acceptance criteria, response time, how to handle errors detected during acceptance","Determine when the project will be completed"],["5. Ownership","Source code, design, domain name, hosting, data, admin account belongs to whom and since when","Decide whether the business actually owns a website or not"],["6. Handover","List of delivered assets: source code, accounts, documentation, server information","Enough to operate yourself or change units when needed"],["7. Warranty","Term, scope, response time, what is not covered by the warranty","Avoid arguing when there are errors after handover"],["8. Change scope","How to propose, evaluate, quote costs, approve changes and influence progress","Control costs incurred"],["9. Information security","Responsibility for keeping data, accounts, and business information confidential","Protect business and customer data"],["10. Termination and Disputes","Termination conditions, payment for completed work, handover of unfinished work, dispute resolution","There is a clear way out if cooperation does not meet expectations"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Scope of work: the most important term"},{type:"p",text:"Many disagreements stem from the two sides understanding the scope differently. Businesses think sales websites include online payments and shipping connections; The website maker understands it's just a shopping cart and basic ordering. The way to avoid this is to include the scope in a **detailed appendix** including:"},{type:"ul",items:["Site map and short description of each page.","List of functions, including what is **not included**.","Number of rounds of design and programming revisions in scope.","Which party prepares the content and images; If the website maker writes, what pages should be written?","Third-party integrations such as payments, shipping, CRM, and account eligibility are required."]},{type:"h2",text:"Ownership and handover: don't leave it ambiguous"},{type:"p",text:"A website is only an asset of a business when the core components are in the name of the business. The contract should clearly state:"},{type:"ol",items:["**Domain name** is registered in the correct business name, the business holds a management account.","**Hosting or server** is in the name of the business, or there is a commitment to transfer when the business requests.","**Source code** is delivered in full, usually after completing payment according to the contract.","**Data** of customers, orders, and content belongs to the business and can be exported when needed.","The highest-level **admin account** belongs to the business, with user manuals included.","**Third party copyright**: themes, plugins, fonts, images have a valid license, clearly stating who pays the renewal fee."]},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"Example from Xartisan Studio",text:"At Xartisan Studio, the source code, domain name, data and administrative account are in the name of the customer business. Warranty policy includes free correction within the accepted scope for 5 years (60 months) and lifetime warranty against errors caused by Xartisan Studio; New features or changes beyond the scope of the cost are quoted in advance."},{type:"h2",text:"Warranty and change scope"},{type:"p",text:"Warranty terms should answer three questions: **how long is the warranty, what does it include, and how to report errors**. A warranty line that only states the duration without stating the scope is almost worthless in the event of a dispute. Three types of requests should be clearly distinguished: errors caused by the web developer, edits within the accepted scope, and new requests outside the scope."},{type:"p",text:"With scope changes, the reasonable process is: the business proposes in writing, the web unit evaluates and reports costs and time, both parties confirm and then deploy. This process protects businesses from unexpected events, and also helps web developers avoid having to do extra work that is not recognized."},{type:"h2",text:"Warning signs in contracts"},{type:"ul",items:["There is no scope appendix, just a general statement that website design is required.","Do not mention source code, domain name, admin account.","Full payment required before any products are available for approval.","The warranty does not state the scope, or is called maintenance but is actually a mandatory annual fee with no clear details.","Commit to specific Google rankings, for example reaching top 1 in a short time.","There is no termination or handover clause upon termination of cooperation."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"The article is for reference only",text:"The above content helps you know what to ask and is not a substitute for legal advice. For large value contracts or special terms, ask someone with legal expertise to review them before signing."},{type:"h2",text:"Before signing, review together"},{type:"p",text:"A contract review with the web company, going over each clause, often helps uncover areas of understanding between the two parties before they become problems. Serious units will be ready to explain and adjust unclear points. Refer to Xartisan Studio's [working process from request to handover](/quy-trinh-thiet-ke-website), [warranty and handover policy](/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website), or read [9 criteria for evaluating website design units](/blog/chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-reputation)."},{type:"p",text:"A good contract is like the paperwork for an asset: it defines what the asset includes, who it belongs to, and how it will be cared for. If you would like to see a quote with scope, title and warranty clearly stated, please [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he)."}],faq:[{question:"Do I need to sign a contract to build a website?",answer:"There should be. A contract, or at least a quote with a scope addendum confirmed by both parties, helps avoid misunderstandings about work, costs, time, ownership and warranties."},{question:"How many installments should I pay?",answer:"Usually divided by work milestones, for example, deposit at the beginning, further payment upon design approval or completion of programming, and the remainder upon acceptance. It is important that each batch is tied to a specific outcome."},{question:"When is the source code delivered?",answer:"Normally after completing payment according to the contract. The contract should clearly state the time, form of handover and a list of what is handed over."},{question:"How to handle changes in requirements midway?",answer:"Changes within the agreed scope are processed according to the number of revision rounds in the contract. New requests that are out of scope should be evaluated, cost and time quoted, and both parties confirmed before implementation."},{question:"Is there a standard website design contract template?",answer:"There is no one right model for every project. You can use the checklist in the article to check whether the contract includes all important clause groups, and ask someone with legal expertise to review it when necessary."}]},{slug:"ten-mien-va-hosting-cho-doanh-nghiep",title:"Domain name and hosting: how to choose, whose name is in, how to renew?",metaTitle:"Domain name and hosting for businesses: choose, register, renew | Xartisan Studio",description:"Easy-to-understand instructions on domain names and hosting for businesses: how to choose a domain name, whether to use.vn or.com, choose the type of hosting, why it is necessary to name the business and how to not forget to renew.",keywords:["domain name and hosting","choose domain name","What is hosting?",".vn domain name","domain name renewal"],category:"Basic knowledge",tags:["Domain name","Hosting","Ownership"],date:"2026-07-08",updated:"2026-07-10",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"Domain name is the address, hosting is the place where the website is located. These are two small things, but if you choose the wrong one, use the wrong name or forget to renew, the business can lose both the website and the address it has built online.",ctaService:"/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website",related:["bao-mat-website-ssl-sao-luu-cap-nhat","hop-dong-thiet-ke-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"When making a website, the first two concepts you will hear are **domain name** and **hosting**. They are often seen as technical details for the website developer to take care of, but in fact these are the two most important components of website ownership. Choosing a domain name that is difficult to remember, leaving the domain name in someone else's name or forgetting to renew it can cause a business to lose the address it has built for many years. The article explains what you need to know in the easiest way to understand."},{type:"h2",text:"What are domain names and hosting?"},{type:"p",text:"Imagine your website as a store. **Domain name** is the address of the store, for example tencongty.vn, for customers to type in and find. **Hosting** is the premises where the store is located: the server stores source code, images, data and returns the content to the customer's browser. These two are purchased separately, possibly from two different vendors, and are connected to each other via DNS configuration."},{type:"table",headers:["Criteria","Domain name","Hosting"],rows:[["Role","Address for visitors to find the website","Where to store and operate the website"],["How to pay fees","By year, it is possible to register for many years at a time","Monthly or yearly depending on package"],["If expired","The website is inaccessible, the domain name may be registered by someone else","Website stops working, data may be deleted after a period of time"],["Change supplier","To transfer, you need management rights and domain name transfer code","Transferable, need to backup and reconfigure"]]},{type:"h2",text:"How to choose the right domain name?"},{type:"ul",items:["**Short, easy to read, easy to remember**: prioritize brand name; Avoid strings that are too long or contain many hyphens.","**Easy to read over the phone**: try reading the domain name to someone else; If they have to ask again how to write, consider another option.","**Avoid names that are easily confused** with other brands or identical to registered trademarks.","**Register additional important extensions** to protect the brand, for example.vn,.com.vn and.com, then redirect to the main domain name."]},{type:"p",text:"**Should you choose.vn or.com?** If customers are mainly in Vietnam, the.vn or.com.vn extension helps identify Vietnamese businesses and is familiar to domestic customers. If going international,.com is more popular. Many businesses register both to avoid being taken over by someone else..vn domain names are registered through registrars recognized by VNNIC and require accurate subject information that matches the documents."},{type:"h2",text:"In whose name: rules cannot be compromised"},{type:"p",text:"The domain name and hosting must be in the name of the business, not the personal name of an employee, and not the name of the web company. The person in whose name is the person who has the final decision on the asset: renewal, change of supplier, change of configuration, even transfer."},{type:"ul",items:["Use **company's general email** to register an account, do not use the personal email of someone who may quit their job.","Register a domain name using the business's legal entity information, keep invoices and registration documents.","Store your domain management, hosting, and DNS account information in a safe place where at least two authorized people know how to access it.","Enable two-factor authentication for domain management and hosting accounts, along with other protection layers in the article [website security](/blog/bao-mat-website-ssl-sao-luu-cap-nhat)."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Common situations",text:"The former employee registered the domain name using personal email and then quit, or the web company kept the domain name and asked for a fee to transfer it back. Both cause businesses to lose control of their own assets. Please check the current domain registration information immediately."},{type:"h2",text:"Choose the right type of hosting"},{type:"table",headers:["Hosting type","Fits","Note"],rows:[["Shared hosting (shared)","Small introduction website, rarely visited","Low cost, but shares resources with many other websites"],["VPS (virtual private server)","Business website, medium-sized sales website","Own resources, need technical administrator"],["Cloud or managed server","High traffic website, web app, needs flexible expansion","High performance and stability, requires thorough configuration"]]},{type:"p",text:"In addition to configuration, ask: **where is the server located** (closer to the customer is faster, can incorporate CDN), **is there automatic backup and how long**, **how does technical support respond when there is a problem**, and **cost of renewal from the second year**. Unusually cheap hosting often comes with limited resources or poor support."},{type:"h2",text:"Renewal: don't lose your asset because you forgot it once"},{type:"ol",items:["**Enable automatic renewal** and attach a valid payment method.","**Multi-year registration** for primary domain to reduce risk of forgetting.","**Set a reminder** at least 30 days before the expiration date, send to at least two people.","**Check your supplier's email for notifications** is still active and does not fall into spam.","**Centralized recording** of domain, hosting, SSL certificate, domain email expiration dates in one tracking table."]},{type:"p",text:"After expiration, the domain name usually has a waiting period before being deleted and opened for registration by someone else. Specific regulations vary by domain extension and provider, and restoration costs during this period can be much higher than normal renewal fees."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Check in 5 minutes",text:"Log in to your provider account, see whose name the domain name is in, what date it expires, and whether automatic renewal has been enabled. If you can't log in, that's what needs to be handled first."},{type:"h2",text:"List needed when handing over"},{type:"ul",items:["Domain name management account at the registrar, with information about the registrant.","Hosting or server management account and technical access information.","Current DNS configuration, including website pointing, email, and service verification records.","Expiry date and renewal fee calculation for each service.","Invoices and registration documents in the name of the enterprise."]},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio hands over or transfers domain names, hosting, administrative accounts and related services to customer businesses. If you want someone to help you, the Basic operating package includes managed hosting, domain name and SSL certificate, so renewals don't depend on one person's memory."},{type:"p",text:"Domain name and hosting are the foundation of website assets. With the correct name, regular renewals, and someone watching, you will avoid having to rebuild from scratch just because of a small detail. See [handover and warranty policy](/bao-hanh-bao-tri-website), [monthly operating packages](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website), or [contact Xartisan Studio](/lien-he) if you need to check the current domain information."}],faq:[{question:"Do domain names and hosting need to be purchased from the same place?",answer:"Not required. Can be purchased from two different providers and connected via DNS. It is important that the business is in its name and holds the management accounts of both."},{question:"Does registering a.vn domain name require documents?",answer:"Have..vn domain names need accurate subject information, matching the documents of the individual or organization registering. Businesses should register using the company's legal entity information."},{question:"If I forget to renew my domain name, can I get it back?",answer:"There is usually a recovery period after expiration, but there may be additional fees and the website may be down in the meantime. If left too long, the domain name may be deleted and someone else may register it."},{question:"Does a small website need VPS?",answer:"Usually not needed. Good quality shared hosting is enough for referral websites with little traffic. When your website has a lot of traffic, a lot of sales, or needs special configuration, you should upgrade to VPS or cloud."},{question:"How to transfer domain name from old unit to business?",answer:"Request the old unit to update subject information to the business or provide a domain name transfer code to transfer to an account managed by the business. Before transferring, you should save your DNS configuration so that your website and email are not interrupted."}]},{slug:"website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi",title:"What pages do a business website need? Standard structure for customers to trust and contact",metaTitle:"What pages do a business website need? Standard structure 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"List of pages needed on the business website: home page, introduction, services, projects, blog, contact, policies. Objectives, required content for each page, and a sample structure diagram.",keywords:["What pages do a business website need?","corporate website structure","sitemap website","corporate website design"],category:"Basic knowledge",tags:["Website structure","Enterprise","Sitemap"],date:"2026-07-01",updated:"2026-07-03",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"A business website doesn't need many pages, but it does need the right pages. These are the pages you should have, what purpose each page serves, and the content required for customers to trust and contact you.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep",related:["viet-noi-dung-website","website-chuan-seo-la-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Before discussing colors or effects, the first question when making a business website is: **what pages does the website need to have**. Page structure determines whether visitors can find the information they need, whether Google understands what the business does, and whether the website is easy to expand in the future. Without important pages, customers lack a basis to believe; Too much unnecessary equipment means the customer will get lost. This article lists the recommended pages, the goal of each page, and a sample structure diagram."},{type:"h2",text:"Core pages of a business website"},{type:"table",headers:["Trang","Objective","Required content"],rows:[["Home","Let customers know immediately what the business does, for whom, and why they should choose it","Key messages, featured services, evidence, calls to contact"],["Introduction","Build trust in people and legal entities","Studio information, years of operation, team, working style, commitment"],["Service or product","Explain in detail each thing the business offers","Each service has its own page: problems, solutions, processes, frequently asked questions"],["Project or customer","Prove your ability by what you have done","Problem, scope, images, deliverables"],["Blog or knowledge","Attract customers from Google, answer questions before buying","Useful article based on real questions from guests"],["Contact","Help customers contact via the most convenient channel","Phone number, WhatsApp, email, address, map, form, working hours"],["Policy","Transparent and meets legal requirements","Privacy policy, terms, warranty or return if any"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Home: the main door, not where everything is stored"},{type:"p",text:"The homepage needs to answer in the first few seconds: what the business does, who it serves, what's the difference and what the customer should do next. A common mistake is cramming too many slides, effects and news into the homepage, making the page heavy and the main message lost. Think of the homepage as lobby signage: succinctly summarizing and leading visitors to the right service, project, or contact page."},{type:"h2",text:"Why should each service have its own page?"},{type:"p",text:"Many websites combine all services on a single page. This method saves effort but loses both sides: visitors have to skim through unrelated things, and Google has difficulty ranking a page that talks about too many topics. When each service has its own page, you can:"},{type:"ul",items:["Write in depth about the exact problem of the customer group that needs that service.","Optimize titles, descriptions and content for the right search terms.","Set appropriate calls to action for each service.","Measure which services attract the most customers."]},{type:"h2",text:"Sample structure diagram for service business website"},{type:"ol",items:["**Home**: summary and navigation.","**Introduction**: story, team, legal, work process.","**Services**: dashboard leading to each subservice page.","**Projects**: list of projects, one detailed page for each project.","**Blog**: categories by groups of guests' questions.","**Contact**: with form, map, messaging channels.","**Policy pages**: privacy, terms, warranty, located in the footer."]},{type:"p",text:"The main menu should be compact, usually about 5 to 7 items; Policy pages are located in the footer. Paths should be short, meaningful and reflect structure, for example /dich-vu/name-dich-vu, helping both visitors and Google understand where the page is located on the website."},{type:"h2",text:"Small but often forgotten pages"},{type:"ul",items:["**Thank you page** after submitting the form: confirms with the customer, indicates when they will be contacted, and is also a reliable conversion measurement point.","**Friendly 404 page**: when visitors land on an incorrect link, take them to the home or service page instead of a blank error page.","**Frequently asked questions page**: collects common concerns about process, costs, and warranty.","**Recruitment page**: if the business is expanding, this page is also proof that the business is growing.","**Competency profile page**: useful when business customers need appraisal before working."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Start with how customers make decisions",text:"List the questions customers often ask before choosing you, then make sure each question has a page or section of content to answer. A good structure is one that follows the customer journey, not the company's organizational chart."},{type:"h2",text:"Good structure helps with SEO and future expansion"},{type:"p",text:"A clear structure from the beginning helps Google crawl and understand your website more easily, and helps you add new services, projects or articles without having to completely rearrange it. On the contrary, websites that lack structure often have to be redone as the business grows. See more [12 criteria for a standard SEO website](/blog/website-chuan-seo-la-gi) and how to [write website content for customers to trust and contact](/blog/viet-noi-dung-website)."},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"No need to do it all at once",text:"New businesses can start with a home page, introduction, main service and contact pages, then add projects and blogs once they have real content. It's important that the structure has room for pages that will be added later."},{type:"p",text:"Page structure is the blueprint of a website's assets: done right from the start, each page added later makes the asset more valuable. Refer to [business website design](/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep), see how Xartisan Studio presents [implemented projects](/du-an), or [contact](/lien-he) to sketch out a sitemap for your website."}],faq:[{question:"How many pages does a business website need at least?",answer:"There is no fixed number. At a minimum, there should be a home page, about, services, and contact. The number of pages increases according to the number of services, projects and content the business wants to present."},{question:"Should you make a one-page website for your business?",answer:"A one-page website is suitable for campaigns or very small businesses with only one service. If you have many services and want to be found on Google, a multi-page website with a separate page for each service is more effective."},{question:"Is a privacy policy page necessary?",answer:"When a website collects customer information such as full name, phone number, email, the business should have a privacy policy clearly stating how the information is used. This is both a requirement for transparency and to help customers feel secure in leaving information."},{question:"Is blogging really necessary?",answer:"Not required from the beginning, but very useful if your business wants customers to find you via Google. A blog is only valuable when it is regularly updated with useful content."},{question:"Is there a need to make an English version?",answer:"Only needed when a business has foreign customers or partners. If you do, you should have a quality translation and a technically correct multilingual structure instead of using an automatic translation tool."}]},{slug:"chi-phi-thiet-ke-website",title:"What does the website design cost include? Construction investment and operating costs 2026",metaTitle:"What does the website design cost include? Setup and operation 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"The 2026 website cost includes two parts: one-time construction investment and monthly operating costs. 6 factors that determine costs, often overlooked items and the right way to invest.",keywords:["website design costs","website design price","website operating costs","website maintenance costs"],category:"Costs & quotes",tags:["Cost","Quote","Budget"],date:"2026-06-24",updated:"2026-06-26",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"Most business owners only charge money to build a website and then forget about operating it - a few years later the website degrades and has to be redone. The article breaks down two parts so you know where you are investing.",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-uy-tin","tu-lam-website-hay-thue-thiet-ke"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:'The question "how much does it cost to make a website" usually only counts the initial construction cost. In fact, a website is an asset of a business: it requires a one-time investment to build the right foundation, and regular operating costs so that the asset does not deteriorate and continues to bring in customers.'},{type:"h2",text:"Website costs include two parts"},{type:"p",text:"Clearly separating these two parts helps you make correct comparisons between units and avoid surprises after handover."},{type:"table",headers:["Expenses","Nature","What's included?"],rows:[["Construction investment (Setup)","Once","Clarify goals, content structure, design, programming, platform technical SEO, measurement settings, handover of ownership"],["Monthly operations","Periodically","Monitor, backup, update content, SEO and content growth, conversion optimization, reporting"],["Domain name, hosting","Every year","Payment to the supplier should be in the name of the business"],["Advertisement (if any)","According to the campaign","Budget paid for advertising platform, separate operating fees"]]},{type:"h2",text:"6 factors that determine website design costs"},{type:"ol",items:["**Number of pages and features**: the more pages, forms, filters, user accounts, the higher the volume.","**Design your own or use an existing template**: designing an interface according to your brand takes more effort than replacing the logo in a template.","**Third-party integration**: payments, shipping, CRM, e-invoicing all incur development and testing time.","**Content and images**: If you need to write content, take photos, or design banners, the cost will increase compared to customers providing it themselves.","**Technical SEO standards and speed**: optimizing structure, schema, and performance requires more methodical techniques.","**Warranty and handover**: long warranty policy, clear source code handover reflects the service value."]},{type:"h2",text:"Hidden costs are rarely reported in advance"},{type:"ul",items:["Domain name: about 250,000 VND - 750,000 VND/year depending on the extension.","Hosting or server: several hundred thousand to several million/year depending on traffic.","SSL certificate: many places are free, some advanced types have a fee.","Operating costs after handover: no one takes care of the website, the website slows down, the content gets old and stops serving customers."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Compare ranges before comparing prices",text:"Low prices do not by themselves guarantee quality, just as high prices do not by themselves guarantee results. Please clearly state the number of pages, functions, administrative rights, source code, maintenance costs and post-handover support conditions."},{type:"h2",text:"How to optimize your budget while still being effective?"},{type:"ul",items:["Start with core scope (MVP), expand features in stages as operational data becomes available.","Prepare content, images and information to reduce costs and shorten time.","Prioritize pages that generate conversions first, such as service pages and contact pages."]},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio does not list a common number because each business has different goals and current status. See [Setup Package model and monthly operating package](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website), then text WhatsApp 0435 878 929 to receive a separate quote for your website."}],faq:[{question:"Why doesn't Xartisan Studio publicize prices?",answer:"Because the cost depends on the goals, number of pages, functions, content and current status of each business. A common number can easily make you make wrong comparisons. Xartisan Studio discusses first and then quotes separately, clearly stating each item."},{question:"Is it mandatory to use the monthly operating package?",answer:"Not required. The website is still owned by you after handover. The operating package is for businesses that want someone to regularly monitor, update and develop their website so it brings in customers."},{question:"Does the price include domain name and hosting?",answer:"Normally domain and hosting are separate costs owned by the customer. The quote will clearly state what is included and what is additional."},{question:"Will it cost more money if I want to add features later?",answer:"Features outside the scope of initial acceptance will be evaluated and costed before implementation."}]},{slug:"landing-page-la-gi",title:"What is a landing page? When to use it and how to optimize conversions",metaTitle:"What is a landing page? How to optimize conversions 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"What is a landing page, how is it different from a regular website, when should you use it, and how to structure a landing page that converts well. Easy-to-understand instructions for newbies.",keywords:["What is a landing page?","landing page","landing page design","conversion optimization"],category:"Basic knowledge",tags:["Landing page","Convert","Advertisement"],date:"2026-06-22",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"Landing page is a page designed for a single goal. Understanding it correctly helps you run ads much more effectively.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-landing-page",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","website-chuan-seo-la-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"When running an advertising campaign, viewers need to go to a page with information that matches the message they just clicked on. Landing pages help focus content and measure a specific action of the campaign."},{type:"h2",text:"What is a landing page?"},{type:"p",text:"Landing page (landing page) is an independent website designed around **a single conversion goal**: leaving a phone number, sending a WhatsApp message, registering for consultation or making a purchase. Unlike the homepage, which has many directions, a landing page only guides viewers to one action."},{type:"h2",text:"How is a landing page different from a regular website?"},{type:"table",headers:["Criteria","Landing page","Regular website"],rows:[["Objective","One single action","Multiple goals"],["Page number","Usually one page long","Many pages"],["Navigation menu","Minimalist or hidden","Full"],["Used for","Advertising campaign","Long-lasting brand"]]},{type:"h2",text:"When should you use a landing page?"},{type:"ul",items:["Run ads for a specific product, service or offer.","Launch new products or organize limited-time events.","Collect leads (registration, receiving documents, scheduling).","Introduce a real estate project, course or sales combo."]},{type:"h2",text:"Structure a landing page that converts well"},{type:"ol",items:["**Strong headline**: clearly states the main benefit in the first few seconds.","**Problem and solution**: touch the customer's pain and then provide the solution.","**Proof**: real pictures, feedback, verifiable numbers.","**Clear call to action (CTA)** is clear, repeated in multiple locations.","**Concise form** and call/WhatsApp button are easy to operate on the phone."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Little tip",text:"Each landing page should only have one main CTA. The more options, the more likely it is that viewers will be confused and leave."},{type:"p",text:"If the campaign needs a separate landing page, see [landing page design scope](/thiet-ke-landing-page) and agree on content, tracking and goals before running ads."}],faq:[{question:"Can landing pages do SEO?",answer:"On-page and index optimization is possible, but a single page cannot replace a multi-page website strategy for long-term SEO."},{question:"How long does it take to make a landing page?",answer:"Usually 3 to 5 days depending on the complexity of the content, effects and measurement integration."},{question:"Can Google Analytics and Pixel be attached?",answer:"Have. Landing pages should have tracking configured before running ads to measure effectiveness."}]},{slug:"website-chuan-seo-la-gi",title:"What is an SEO standard website? 12 inspection criteria before handover",metaTitle:"What is an SEO standard website? 12 necessary criteria 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"What is a standard SEO website and what criteria does it include? 12 technical, structural and experience checkpoints help your website get to the top more easily.",keywords:["SEO standard website","What is SEO?","SEO standard website criteria","SEO standard web design"],category:"SEO & optimization",tags:["SEO","Technical","Optimal"],date:"2026-06-20",readingMinutes:9,excerpt:"Many places advertise 'SEO standard websites' but rarely say clearly what they are. Here are 12 specific criteria you can check for yourself.",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","landing-page-la-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"The phrase 'SEO website' appears in most web design quotes, but what does it really mean? Understanding correctly helps you evaluate whether the product you receive has a good foundation or not."},{type:"h2",text:"What is an SEO standard website?"},{type:"p",text:"An SEO standard website is a website built to be **easy for search engines to crawl, understand and rank**, while also providing a good user experience. Note: technical SEO standards are a necessary condition, not a promise to reach the top, because rankings also depend on content, reputation and competitors."},{type:"h2",text:"12 criteria of a standard SEO website"},{type:"ol",items:["Clean URL structure, hyphens, no parameters.","Each page has its own title tag and meta description.","The H1, H2, H3 heading system is reasonable according to the content.","Fast page loading speed, optimized images and source code.","Responsive, displays well on phones (mobile-first).","Have sitemap.xml and robots.txt file configured correctly.","Structured data (schema) for businesses, products, articles.","Canonical tag to avoid duplicate content.","Internal links between related pages.","Images have alt attributes that accurately describe the content.","Secure HTTPS link with SSL certificate.","Stable indexing ability, does not mistakenly block search engines."]},{type:"h2",text:"How are technical SEO standards different from SEO?"},{type:"p",text:"Technical SEO standards are the foundation that the web design unit undertakes upon handover. And **doing SEO** is a long process: keyword research, content production, link building and improving based on data. A website with good technical background will make the future SEO process much easier."},{type:"callout",variant:"info",title:"Quick check",text:"You can use Google Search Console and PageSpeed Insights (both free) to self-assess most of the technical criteria above."},{type:"p",text:"If you need to evaluate your current website, see [scope of SEO website](/dich-vu-seo-website) including technical audit, content structure and data prioritization plan."}],faq:[{question:"Is a SEO standard website sure to reach the top of Google?",answer:"Are not. Technical SEO standards are just the foundation. Ranking depends on content, domain authority, backlinks and competition level."},{question:"How long does it take for a new website to rank?",answer:"It usually takes several months for Google to trust a new domain name, along with ongoing content and optimization."},{question:"Is it necessary to do separate SEO after web design?",answer:"Have. SEO standard design is the foundation step; If you want to compete for keywords, you need to deploy content and optimize periodically."}]},{slug:"tu-lam-website-hay-thue-thiet-ke",title:"Should I make my own website or hire a design unit? Compare details",metaTitle:"Make your own website or hire a designer? Compare 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"Compare making your own website (WordPress, Wix) and hiring a design unit: cost, time, scalability and risks. Helps you choose the right one.",keywords:["make your own website","Hire website design","design your own website","wix wordpress"],category:"Experience in choosing services",tags:["Compare","Decision","DIY"],date:"2026-06-18",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"Making your own website saves money but is time consuming and prone to limitations. When should you do it yourself, when should you hire?",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-uy-tin"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"With drag and drop platforms like Wix, WordPress or Canva, anyone can build a simple website. But is DIY really right for you? Consider both directions."},{type:"h2",text:"Making your own website: pros and cons"},{type:"ul",items:["**Advantages**: low cost, proactive editing, suitable for simple or experimental needs.","**Disadvantages**: takes a lot of time to learn, interface easily resembles a template, limited advanced features, difficult to optimize speed and technical SEO."]},{type:"h2",text:"Hiring a design unit: pros and cons"},{type:"ul",items:["**Advantages**: brand-specific interface, technical optimization, time saving, warranty and support.","**Disadvantages**: higher cost than doing it yourself, requires time to discuss clear requirements."]},{type:"h2",text:"Quick comparison"},{type:"table",headers:["Criteria","Do it yourself","Hire a designer"],rows:[["Initial cost","Low","Higher"],["Your time","It costs a lot","Savings"],["Custom design","Limitations","By brand"],["Scalability","Limit","Flexible"],["Technical support","Manage yourself","Warranty available"]]},{type:"h2",text:"So which way should you choose?"},{type:"p",text:"If you need a simple site, have a very limited budget, and have time to learn on your own, do it yourself. If your website is your main business channel and needs professional images and scalability, hiring a design unit will be more economical in the long run. You can refer to [custom website design service](/thiet-ke-website) and [price list](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website) to compare with the cost of doing it yourself."}],faq:[{question:"Can people who are not tech savvy make their own website?",answer:"Yes with basic drag and drop platforms, but it will take time and difficulty reaching the optimal level like a professional unit."},{question:"After hiring a designer, can I edit it myself?",answer:"Yes, if the administration page and instructions for use are handed over. Please confirm this in the quote."},{question:"What are the disadvantages of making your own website for free?",answer:"Often includes subdomains, platform ads, limited features, and you don't actually own the infrastructure."}]},{slug:"thiet-ke-website-ban-hang-can-gi",title:"What is needed to design a sales website? Full checklist",metaTitle:"What is needed to design a sales website? Checklist 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"Checklist for designing a sales website: core features, preparation work and common mistakes that make the website difficult to sell.",keywords:["Sales website design","What do you need for a sales website?","Make a sales website","ecommerce"],category:"Basic knowledge",tags:["Sales","Checklist","E-commerce"],date:"2026-06-17",readingMinutes:8,excerpt:"A good sales website needs more than just a product list. Here is the complete checklist before starting work.",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-ban-hang",related:["chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","landing-page-la-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A sales website is not just a place to display products. It must help customers find products quickly, buy conveniently and help you manage orders neatly. Here's what you need."},{type:"h2",text:"Core features of sales website"},{type:"ul",items:["Categorize and filter products the way customers actually search.","Product pages have images, variations (color, size), prices and clear descriptions.","The shopping cart and ordering process are concise.","Many forms of payment: COD, bank transfer, payment gateway.","Order, customer and inventory management pages.","Optimize purchases on the phone."]},{type:"h2",text:"Checklist to prepare before work"},{type:"ol",items:["Product listing, images and variant information.","How to group categories and inventory logic.","Desired payment and reconciliation method.","Shipping, return and service area policies.","Store contact and legal information."]},{type:"h2",text:"Common mistakes"},{type:"ul",items:["Stuffing too many steps in the payment process causes customers to abandon their carts.","Blurry product images, lack of description, lack of price.","Not optimized for phones even though most customers buy on mobile.","Ignore product SEO so no one can find the product through Google."]},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Suggestion",text:"Start with the core feature set, put it into practice, then expand (discount codes, points, multiple warehouses) once you have customer data."},{type:"p",text:"See details of [sales website design service](/thiet-ke-website-ban-hang) of Xartisan Studio, or refer to [implemented projects](/du-an) for a clearer picture."}],faq:[{question:"Can the sales website integrate shipping units?",answer:"API connection is possible if the carrier supports it and your account is eligible. Range is confirmed before quoting."},{question:"Is there inventory management by variation?",answer:"Have. Inventory can be managed by product or by variation such as color and size."},{question:"How long does it take to create a sales website?",answer:"Depending on product quantity and features. Sales projects are often scheduled after detailed requirements are analyzed."}]},{slug:"chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-uy-tin",title:"9 criteria for evaluating website design units for businesses",metaTitle:"9 criteria for evaluating website design units in 2026 | Xartisan Studio",description:"Nine criteria for businesses to evaluate website design partners: capacity, project, quote, ownership, security and operational support.",keywords:["reputable website design unit","web design company","Choose a web design unit","Reputable web design"],category:"Experience in choosing services",tags:["Choose","Prestigious","Experience"],date:"2026-06-16",readingMinutes:7,excerpt:"A checklist for the team to evaluate capacity, scope of delivery and working style before choosing a website partner.",ctaService:"/gioi-thieu",related:["tu-lam-website-hay-thue-thiet-ke","chi-phi-thiet-ke-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"The website will be associated with the brand, data and operating procedures of the business for many years. The following set of criteria helps the team evaluate implementation capacity, working style, ownership and scope of support before choosing a partner."},{type:"h2",text:"9 criteria for evaluating reputable website design units"},{type:"ol",items:["**Clear legal entity**: has transparent company name, tax code, address and contact information.","**Real Portfolio**: completed projects that are still active, accessible and verifiable.","**Transparent quote**: clearly state the scope of work, output, time and exclusions.","**Handover of source code**: you own the source code, admin account and domain name.","**Clear process**: from request receipt to acceptance, there are specific milestones.","**Warranty policy**: commitment to handle technical errors within a specified time.","**Consulting on demand**: ask about business goals instead of just offering cheap packages.","**Professional feedback**: clear communication, on time, in writing.","**Reviews from previous customers**: real, referenceable feedback."]},{type:"h2",text:"Warning signs to avoid"},{type:"ul",items:["The price is unusually cheap but the range is not specified.","Do not show the real project or avoid questions about the source code.","Commitment to 'top 1 Google after 1 month' for competitive keywords.","The contract is vague, does not clearly state ownership and warranty."]},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Important note",text:"No unit controls Google's algorithm. Be cautious with any commitment to absolute rankings."},{type:"p",text:"You can learn more about [Xartisan Studio](/gioi-thieu), see [public projects](/du-an) or [contact consulting](/lien-he) to discuss directly about your project."}],faq:[{question:"How do you know if your portfolio is a real project?",answer:"Please request a working website link and check directly. Reputable units are ready to provide."},{question:"Is it necessary to hand over source code?",answer:"Highly recommended. Owning source code helps you proactively maintain, upgrade or transfer to another unit when needed."},{question:"Should I sign a contract or verbal agreement?",answer:"It is always a good idea to have a document stating the scope, cost, schedule, warranty and ownership to protect both parties."}]},{slug:"website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep",title:"A business website is a digital asset: how to build it for long-term growth",metaTitle:"Website is a digital asset of a business | Xartisan Studio",description:"The website becomes an asset when the business owns the platform, owns the data, measures the results and has an operation plan after handover. Where to start?",keywords:["Website is a digital asset","Website is a business asset","corporate digital assets","business website development"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Digital assets","Strategy","Enterprise"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"A website does not become an asset just because it has been designed and posted online. Businesses need to master the platform, know what goal the website is serving and continue to take care of it after the handover date.",visual:"asset",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep",related:["doanh-nghiep-can-so-huu-gi-sau-khi-lam-website","tam-nhin-website-doanh-nghiep-trong-3-nam","van-hanh-website-nhu-mot-tai-san"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many businesses view a website as a project with an end point: finalizing the interface, accepting it, and then moving on to something else. But a website only begins to create value when customers use it to learn, trust, contact or buy. If after the launch date no one owns the rights to administer, update information or view results, the website can easily become a completed expense rather than an asset being exploited."},{type:"h2",text:"How is a website different from a one-time expense?"},{type:"p",text:"A digital asset can be continuously used, controlled and improved by a business. The website can store official information, introduce capabilities, receive needs, support sales and provide data for the team to understand what customers are interested in. That value doesn't come from the interface alone. It comes from technical foundations, content, data, operations and measurement capabilities."},{type:"table",headers:["Asset class","Role","Questions businesses need to answer"],rows:[["Platform","Domain name, source code, hosting and website structure","Who owns the account and can transfer it when needed?"],["Content","Business information, products, services and projects","Is the content accurate, has usage rights and is someone updating it?"],["Data","Contacts, orders, behavior and traffic sources","How is data collected, stored and decentralized?"],["Operations","Maintenance, updates, support and troubleshooting","Who is responsible and how is work reported?"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Four conditions for a website to be developed long term"},{type:"ol",items:["**Start with business goals**: determine the website to use for customers to assess capacity, find new customers, sell or support internal processes.","**Enterprise holds ownership**: domain name, data, administrative account and source code scope need to be clearly stated in the agreement.","**Get the right measurement**: track meaningful actions like calls, quote requests, orders or registrations, rather than just visits.","**Someone to look after after launch**: update content, stay safe, handle bugs, and prioritize improvements based on real data."]},{type:"p",text:"Not every website has to have many features from the start. A lean, targeted, and scalable platform is often easier to manage than a large, unmanned project. Businesses can see more about [how to allocate the website budget for the first year](/blog/ngan-sach-website-nam-dau) and [pages needed on the business website](/blog/website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi)."},{type:"h2",text:"For example: same website, two different investment methods"},{type:"p",text:"Imagine a construction company wants a website to help investors evaluate their capabilities. If you only focus on creating an eye-catching home page, your project may lack project pages, role information, who is in charge of updating profiles, and how customers can send requests. If the website is considered an asset, the team will organize project data from the beginning, agree on how to review content, and retain administrative rights. Two options may look the same on opening day, but their usability a year later is completely different."},{type:"h2",text:"A set of questions to check the level of initiative"},{type:"ul",items:["Is there someone in the business responsible for goals and posting information?","Are domains, key accounts, contact data, and measurement tools under the company's control?","Can new employees learn how to update the website from the handover document?","When a form has errors or incorrect content, does the team know who to notify and follow up until it is resolved?","Do you periodically review how your website is helping customers and employees?"]},{type:"p",text:"If many answers are left unanswered, the next step is not necessarily to redo the whole thing. You can start by taking an inventory of your accounts, assets, data, and key journeys, then prioritize your biggest risk points. This approach helps decide on repair, maintenance or expansion based on the actual situation."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"A question to start",text:"If you change providers tomorrow, can your business continue to log in, update content, retrieve data and maintain the website? If unclear, clarify ownership and handover before expanding the feature."},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio looks at websites through the full life cycle: building the right foundation, giving ownership, then protecting, preserving and developing. Learn more about [business website design service](/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep) or [Setup and operation model](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website)."}],faq:[{question:"Does the website become an asset after it is posted online?",answer:"Are not. Businesses need to take ownership of governance and data, have trustworthy content, operators, and clear measurement goals."},{question:"Does a business website need to generate direct revenue to be considered an asset?",answer:"Not necessarily. The capacity profile website can support appraisal partners, while the service website can receive requests. Roles and ways to measure effectiveness depend on business goals."},{question:"Where should I start building a asset website?",answer:"Start with the goals, users, and actions the business wants customers to take; then lock in ownership, content, measurement, and operational plans."}]},{slug:"doanh-nghiep-can-so-huu-gi-sau-khi-lam-website",title:"After building a website, what does a business need to own?",metaTitle:"After building a website, what do you need to hand over? | Xartisan Studio",description:"Checklist of website ownership for businesses: domain name, source code, data, administrative accounts, measurement tools, documents and rights to use third-party assets.",keywords:["What does website handover include?","website ownership","Hand over website source code","business website account"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Ownership","Handover","Checklist"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"A well-delivered website helps businesses continue operating or change partners without losing control. This is a list of accounts, data and documents that need to be reviewed.",visual:"ownership",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi","hop-dong-thiet-ke-website"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"The question of handover often arises close to the acceptance date, when the source code and accounts have been created. To avoid depending on an individual or supplier, businesses should unify the list of ownership rights within the project scope. Handover is more than just sending an administrative link; it is the ability to continue to control and operate the asset."},{type:"h2",text:"Checklist of website ownership that needs to be recorded"},{type:"table",headers:["Category","Businesses need to receive or confirm"],rows:[["Domain names and DNS","Title, recovery email, registrar, renewal date and DNS access."],["Hosting or server","Provider, owner account, backup method, restore method, and renewal information."],["Source code","Source code repository or delivered source code package, running and deployment instructions, and scope of usage rights according to the contract."],["Website administration","Primary administrative account, backup account, and instructions for creating or revoking permissions by role."],["Data","How to export data, important data structures, where copies are saved, and who is allowed access."],["Measurement","Ownership of GA4, Search Console, advertising tools, and related integrated accounts."],["Third Party Assets","List of fonts, plugins, libraries, images, paid services and license conditions."],["Documents","Scope of acceptance, administration instructions, implementation information, warranty and support contacts."]]},{type:"h2",text:"Distinguish ownership from access"},{type:"p",text:"It is possible to be granted an account but the business is not yet the account owner. For example, a domain name registered with a provider's personal email address may leave recovery or transfer up to that person. You should use an email managed by the business for the root account, enable appropriate authentication, and only grant enough permissions to each person."},{type:"p",text:"Source code, design, content and third-party licensed software may have different conditions of use. Don't assume that all components transfer the same; Read the terms and clearly state in the contract which part the business owns and which part is granted the right to use."},{type:"h2",text:"The method of acceptance and handover is concise and sufficient"},{type:"ol",items:["Make a list of accounts and people responsible for each item.","Try logging in with your business account, check your recovery email and two-factor authentication if the service supports it.","Try exporting your data or downloading a sample backup to make sure your team knows how to get your assets back.","Ask for guidance on updating content and handling daily tasks.","Record open defects, warranty period and how to request support in writing."]},{type:"h2",text:"Try a handover scenario before signing for acceptance"},{type:"p",text:"A simple test is to assume the person in charge quits today and the current supplier no longer provides support tomorrow. Can a replacement restore domain access? Do you know where the form data is saved? Are there instructions for deploying a new build or restoring a backup? If not, please write down the missing information in the handover record and designate a recipient."},{type:"ul",items:["Save account information in the business's password management system, do not send it scattered through messages.","Record the account owner and the person authorized to operate separately.","Try downloading the data or backup once to confirm the format and location.","Check support links, warranty period and covered work limits.","Confirm which assets have recurring charges, renewal dates, and the party responsible for payment."]},{type:"p",text:"When changing providers, do not revoke all old permissions before checking the running system and having a replacement plan. Make a list of dependent services, create new permissions for the receiving party, check operation and then remove permissions that are no longer needed. This way, businesses can maintain service continuity and reduce the risk of losing access due to hasty operations."},{type:"p",text:"If you are preparing a new project, please include this checklist in the scope agreement stage, along with the terms in the article [what is needed in a website design contract](/blog/hop-dong-thiet-ke-website). A [suitable website design unit](/blog/chon-don-vi-thiet-ke-website-uy-tin) will clearly explain how the business retains initiative after handover."}],faq:[{question:"Should businesses register domain names?",answer:"Have. The domain name should be registered with the information and email the business controls, and have someone in charge of renewing and saving recovery information."},{question:"Does every website hand over all source code?",answer:"Source code scope and usage rights depend on contract, technology model and third party component license. Both sides should clearly state before starting."},{question:"Do I need to receive administrative documentation?",answer:"There should be. Documents help business personnel update content and perform daily operations without having to depend on the website builder."}]},{slug:"tam-nhin-website-doanh-nghiep-trong-3-nam",title:"Before creating a website, determine which vision the website needs to serve",metaTitle:"Determine your business website vision before building | Xartisan Studio",description:"Frame questions to identify roles, users, data, and a three-year website roadmap, avoiding choosing interfaces or features before business goals.",keywords:["Business website vision","Website building goals","corporate website strategy","website planning"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Vision","Strategy","Make a plan"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"A website may need to serve many different stages of development. Defining roles in advance helps businesses choose the right platform and avoid investing in unused features.",visual:"vision",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","lo-trinh-phat-trien-website-sau-ban-giao","website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A website can launch in a few months but will stay with the business much longer. So the requirements shouldn't just stop at the question of what the interface will look like. The team needs to envision where the website can help the business go, who will use it, and what might change in the coming years."},{type:"h2",text:"Start with five questions about the future of your website"},{type:"ol",items:["**What do businesses want customers to remember?** The answer helps identify the most important messages, evidence, and content.","**Who are the main users?** Customers, partners, candidates, employees or many groups with different needs.","**What do they need to do on the website?** Research, download documents, send requests, schedule appointments, make purchases or log in to the system.","**What part will the team manage?** Products, projects, articles, price lists, accounts and contact data need someone to be in charge.","**What can be expanded later?** Add languages, branches, categories, integrations, or business processes."]},{type:"h2",text:"Separate the long-term vision from the feature list"},{type:"p",text:"Vision describes the website capabilities needed in the future; The feature list is just one way to realize that capability. For example, if the goal is for multiple departments to update information independently, the core requirement is decentralization and content approval process. A dashboard with many charts may not solve that problem."},{type:"p",text:"Record each idea in three layers: the problem at hand, the person needing support, and the observable outcome. Then classify into things that are needed at launch, things that can be done after having data and ideas that do not require investment. This helps keep the vision intact without turning the first version into an overwhelming project."},{type:"h2",text:"A one-page orientation is enough to get started"},{type:"table",headers:["Section","Content should be written"],rows:[["Objective","Main business role of the website for 12 to 36 months."],["User","The group of customers, partners or people and the questions they want to solve."],["Action","Contact, book an appointment, request a quote, purchase or process."],["Evidence","Projects, certifications, validated metrics, teams or policies."],["Operations","Who updates, who approves, who views reports and who handles problems."],["Phase","Foundations at launch, next expansion steps and conditions for expansion."]]},{type:"h2",text:"Turn your vision into actionable decisions"},{type:"p",text:"For example, a B2B business wants to serve more product groups and customers in new markets in the next few years. Topics should not just be about adding language flags. The team needs to determine who translates and approves the content, which categories need to be separated, what the request form should ask, who handles leads, and how to update product data. The vision becomes specific architectural, content and operational decisions."},{type:"table",headers:["Future ideas","Capacity needs to be prepared","Do it now or leave it later?"],rows:[["Add branch","Location data model and update process","Standardize the structure first; Add more when needed."],["Open more services","Service pages can reuse the same set of content fields","Design the structure from scratch, publishing only active services."],["CRM connection","Classification rules, data fields, and lead recipients","Finalize requests and access before integration."],["Online sales","Categories, prices, inventory, orders and support","Only build when the operating model is ready."]]},{type:"p",text:"You can use three questions to rank order: if not done yet, what obstacles are the customer or team facing; What data or processes prove that the problem is real; And who will operate the feature after construction is complete? Things that are required for the website to be safe, accessible, or to complete the main journey often need to be handled first. It is only useful when the scale increases so there is a trigger condition. Ideas that do not yet have a user or operating owner should be recorded, not included in the initial scope."},{type:"p",text:"For each future feature, write down the trigger condition: increased content volume, a new department to manage, slow manual processes, or the business officially opening a sales channel. If you can't afford it, keep the scalability in the architecture but don't need to pay the cost of building features right away."},{type:"p",text:"Once there is direction, the new team needs to finalize [business website structure](/blog/website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi), scope, budget and implementation plan. Xartisan Studio starts with operational goals and customer journeys before choosing an interface or technology."}],faq:[{question:"Does a small business need to create a website vision?",answer:"Maybe start with a short orientation page. The goal is to know who the website serves, what it solves, and what needs to be expanded in the future."},{question:"Should all the features be done from the beginning for long-term use?",answer:"Not necessarily. It's a good idea to build a scalable foundation, deploy the essentials first, and add features as the process or data justify the need."},{question:"Who should participate in determining website goals?",answer:"There should be someone responsible for business, someone who understands the operating process, someone in charge of content and a technical focal point if the business has one."}]},{slug:"lo-trinh-phat-trien-website-sau-ban-giao",title:"Website development roadmap after handover: from foundation to growth",metaTitle:"Website development roadmap after handover | Xartisan Studio",description:"Websites need to be tested, measured and improved after launch day. This is a phased roadmap for businesses to develop digital assets based on actual needs.",keywords:["Website development after handover","website development roadmap","Operate business website","website after launch"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Route","Operations","Growth"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Launch day is not the finish line. The post-handover roadmap helps businesses keep their websites stable, understand user behavior and choose improvements based on evidence instead of guessing.",visual:"roadmap",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["tam-nhin-website-doanh-nghiep-trong-3-nam","bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi","do-luong-website-ga4-search-console"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Newly launched websites often do not have enough data to know that all initial decisions are correct. Some content needs to be added, customers may stumble at an unanticipated step, and the team needs time to get used to the admin tools. Therefore, prepare a post-handover roadmap before the website goes online."},{type:"h2",text:"Four stages of website asset development"},{type:"table",headers:["Phase","Things to prioritize","Signs to move forward"],rows:[["Launched","Test paths, forms, mobile displays, accounts, backups, and measurement tools.","The main itineraries are operational and the person in charge has received the handover."],["Stable","Track bugs, update information, view landing pages, and periodically try contact.","Website operates stably, measurement data can be used."],["Learn","Find user drop-off points, frequently asked questions, and missing content.","There is evidence on a few priority issues instead of a list of conjectures."],["Grow","Improve content, experiences, processes, or integrations according to business goals.","Changes are tracked to know whether to continue, adjust, or stop."]]},{type:"h2",text:"Choose innovation based on impact and verifiability"},{type:"p",text:"Each month, the team can compile a list of issues, estimate the impact on customers or operations, and then choose a few that can be measured. For example, fix a quote form that's missing necessary information, clarify a service page that has a lot of repeat customers, or improve speed on a high-traffic page. Don't add a feature just because your competitors have one if you don't know what problem that feature solves."},{type:"ul",items:["Keep a change list with who is responsible and deadlines.","Record the status before adjusting for a basis for comparison.","Prioritize errors that impact customers, data, or security.","Separate required maintenance work from growth improvement testing.","Periodically review access rights and backup plans."]},{type:"h2",text:"Suggested work rhythm for the first 90 days"},{type:"table",headers:["Time","Work group","Output needs to be retained"],rows:[["First week","Test forms, contacts, links, mobile display and accounts.","Priority error list, handling recipient and acceptance record are still open."],["Weeks 2 to 4","Review content, request reception process and measurement data.","The passenger itinerary record and questions are missing on the website."],["Second month","Choose one or two improvements that will have a clear impact on guests or the team.","Description of changes, before and after measurements, reviewer."],["Third month","Evaluate results and update the roadmap for the next quarter.","Decide whether to continue, adjust, or stop each test."]]},{type:"p",text:"For example, if many people open a service page but few send requests, don't rush to change the entire interface. First, check the page on your phone, try submitting the form, ask the sales team which questions customers are missing the answer to and see if the traffic source is the right target group. Only when a possible cause is found should a specific change be proposed, record the initial data and then re-evaluate after a sufficient period of time to have the data. If traffic is low, combine quantitative data with interviews and direct feedback."},{type:"p",text:"When there are major changes, prepare a recovery plan: backups, who has deployment rights, and how to test after the update. A change is considered complete when the main flow is tested by the user, critical data is intact, and the operator knows the new state. Here's how to avoid turning your website into an untraceable series of edits."},{type:"p",text:"The roadmap doesn't necessarily have to have a big budget each month. It is important that businesses know what stage the assets are in, who holds responsibility and what information to base their next decisions on. See also [website maintenance checklist](/blog/bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi) and [how to read GA4 with Search Console](/blog/do-luong-website-ga4-search-console)."}],faq:[{question:"How long after launch should you start optimizing your website?",answer:"From the beginning, it is necessary to track errors and key journeys. Changes to content or conversions should be based on enough data appropriate to the traffic and goals of the website."},{question:"Do you need to change the interface regularly for a new website?",answer:"Are not. Changes should be made when there are experience, brand or business goal issues that need to be resolved; No need to refresh just to create a new feeling."},{question:"Who should be responsible for the post-handover roadmap?",answer:"Businesses should designate a focal point to prioritize and coordinate with content, operations, and technical people."}]},{slug:"van-hanh-website-nhu-mot-tai-san",title:"Operate the website like an asset: need someone in charge and a clear working rhythm",metaTitle:"How to operate a website like a business asset | Xartisan Studio",description:"The model assigns responsibilities for content, technology, data and budget so that the website is not forgotten after the handover date.",keywords:["Operate business website","person in charge of the website","Enterprise website management","Maintain website after handover"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Administration","Operations","Responsibility"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Website cannot be taken care of with general responsibility. Businesses need decision-making focal points, content updaters, technical handlers, and appropriate review rhythms.",visual:"stewardship",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","lo-trinh-phat-trien-website-sau-ban-giao","bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"When the website has problems, the familiar answer is that we don't know who is in charge. The content is kept by the sales department, the domain name is registered by someone else, the analytics account is in an old email, and the vendor is only called when there is an error. This is a sign that the website has not been managed as a business asset."},{type:"h2",text:"Assign according to responsibilities, not necessarily by title"},{type:"table",headers:["Responsibility","Main thing","Need to coordinate with"],rows:[["Business owner","Set goals, review priorities, confirm disclosures.","Executive Board and departments."],["Content management","Update services, products, projects, news and documents.","Business, human resources, marketing."],["Technical focal point","Monitor operations, accounts, backups, updates, and troubleshooting.","Hosting provider or developer."],["Data monitor","Review traffic reports, forms, calls and contact quality.","Business and marketing."]]},{type:"p",text:"In a small business, one person can take on many roles. What should be avoided is leaving all responsibilities in the default state, with no replacement when the focal point takes leave or leaves the company. Accounts should use business email, access rights should be granted according to tasks and revoked when personnel change roles."},{type:"h2",text:"Set up an operating rhythm that fits the scale"},{type:"ul",items:["**Weekly**: test important forms, call buttons, orders, or contact flows.","**Monthly**: update content, view technical errors and review data needed for business decisions.","**Quarterly**: evaluate which pages need fixing, which access permissions need to be revoked, and whether backups are recoverable.","**When there is a major change**: record who approved it, when it was deployed, and how to roll back if the update causes errors."]},{type:"h2",text:"For example, a quote form has a submitter but no one processes it"},{type:"p",text:"Suppose the customer still sends a request via the website but the sales team does not see the notification email. The content administrator may think the website is live because the page is still open; Technical people may not know forms are an important lead generation flow. A good operating procedure clearly states who checks the inbox, who tries to send recurring requests, who responds when errors are reported, and who confirms the affected customer has been contacted."},{type:"ol",items:["Record the dates, pages, and contact information affected; Do not post customer data to public communication channels.","Technical liaison checks forms, received emails, mailing services, and error logs.","Sales contact checks outstanding requests and continues to contact customers through appropriate channels.","After fixing, the other person tries the entire stream again on their phone and computer.","Update causes, treatment methods and preventive steps in the operational monitoring book."]},{type:"p",text:"Businesses do not necessarily need to buy a complex administration system to get started. A tracking sheet with columns for date recorded, impact level, handler, status, and retest results helped prevent many missed tasks. As the number of requests or integrations increases, the team can move the process into the appropriate management tool."},{type:"h2",text:"Website review form in monthly meeting"},{type:"ul",items:["Important incidents or requests during the month: impact, cause, handler and open tasks.","Content status: what information has changed, what pages need approval, who is responsible for confirmation.","Targeted results: what metrics matter, data limitations, and customer contact feedback.","Next month's priorities: at least a few tasks with people to do them, deadlines and how to approve them.","Permissions and recurring costs: accounts to review, upcoming license renewals, and most recent backups."]},{type:"p",text:"The meeting does not need to be long if the focal points are updated on the status of the work in advance. The value of a review cadence is to create ownership of decisions: what gets done, what gets postponed, who needs what information, and when to check the results. If the website serves an important transaction or process, more careful monitoring may be needed according to the level of risk rather than waiting until the monthly meeting."},{type:"p",text:"This rhythm can be adjusted according to the importance of the website. A website that introduces information that rarely changes will need to operate differently than a store that has orders every day. The article [what does website maintenance include](/blog/bao-tri-website-gom-nhung-gi) delves into technical tasks; The article [measuring websites using GA4 and Search Console](/blog/do-luong-website-ga4-search-console) helps determine what data to look at."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"Simple governance rules",text:"Every important task needs a main person in charge, an alternate person, and a way to hand over access rights. This way the website will still be taken care of when the team changes."}],faq:[{question:"Does a small business need a dedicated employee for the website?",answer:"Not necessarily. It is possible to assign concurrent roles, as long as the decision maker, update person, technical monitor and replacement person are clear."},{question:"Who should hold the highest admin account?",answer:"Owner accounts should be controlled by the business via company email and recovery information. The supplier is granted the necessary permissions to perform the work."},{question:"Should we outsource all website operations?",answer:"Technical or content can be rented, but the business should still retain ownership of the account, data, and prioritization decisions."}]},{slug:"do-luong-hieu-qua-website-bang-ket-qua-kinh-doanh",title:"Measure website effectiveness by business results, not just by visits",metaTitle:"Measure website effectiveness by customers and business results | Xartisan Studio",description:"Choose website metrics according to goals: consultation requests, calls, orders, lead quality and contribution to the sales process.",keywords:["Measure website effectiveness","Evaluate the effectiveness of business websites","Website index needs to be monitored","website brings customers"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Measurement","Kinh doanh","Convert"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Visits indicate that there are people visiting the website, but it does not say whether they are the right audience or whether they create business opportunities. Connect website metrics to the goals your team really needs.",visual:"measure",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["do-luong-website-ga4-search-console","website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","ngan-sach-website-nam-dau"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A report with many charts may still not help a business know how the website is working. Views increase but the form is not submitted, the call is not recorded or the lead is not suitable, the number of visits alone is not enough to evaluate effectiveness."},{type:"h2",text:"Start from the action the website needs to create"},{type:"p",text:"Choose a primary target according to website role: customer requests consultation, distributor downloads application, buyer completes application, candidate submits application or employee handles a faster process. Then agree on how to record that action, who is responsible and how to connect the data to the sales system if any."},{type:"table",headers:["Objective","Metrics to track","Next question"],rows:[["Receive consultation requests","Number of successfully submitted forms, calls or contacts via WhatsApp.","How many requests are suitable for the service?"],["Create sales opportunities","Number of qualified leads and their traffic sources.","Which groups of customers come forward for appointments or quotes?"],["Online sales","Application completed, order value, customer exits the process.","Which product pages or checkout steps need improvement?"],["Support business appraisal","Capacity, project, profile pages are viewed or downloaded.","What proof do customers need before contacting?"],["Reduce internal operations","Processing time, re-entry, and process errors.","Which step is causing slow or incorrect data?"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Connect website data with sales results"},{type:"p",text:"If possible, each request should retain the customer source and processing status after being passed to the sales team. At that time, the business not only knows how many people clicked send, but also knew which requests were contacted, became opportunities or were not suitable. It is necessary to unify the definition between the website and CRM so that the same type of conversion is not counted differently."},{type:"h2",text:"A simple set of indicators to get started"},{type:"p",text:"No need for a multi-level dashboard. Agree a funnel in advance that is sufficient to detect bottlenecks: relevant page visits → successful contact action → confirmed request → request meets business criteria → opportunity to progress to an appointment or quote. Each step requires a shared definition, a data source, and a person responsible for testing."},{type:"table",headers:["Index","Suggested calculation method","Things to check"],rows:[["Request submission success rate","Number of successful submissions ÷ number of landing page views","Does the event fire once and only after successful submission?"],["Appropriate request rate","Requests meeting agreed criteria ÷ total requests received","Are the eligibility criteria clear and consistently applied?"],["On-time response rate","Request responded to within internal deadline ÷ request needs response","Which deadline is consistent with the business's customer care commitment?"],["Percentage of progress to sales","Request an appointment or quote ÷ request accordingly","Can the sales data source be reconnected to the original customer source?"]]},{type:"p",text:"The above formulas are a management framework, not an industry standard to compare all businesses. If traffic is low, a few change requests will cause the rate to fluctuate widely; Then you should consider the absolute quantity, the content of the exchange, and the long enough period of time. Don't optimize a form just to increase submissions if your team gets more requests than it can handle."},{type:"h2",text:"Set up measurements to avoid wrong decisions"},{type:"ul",items:["Test events on real devices, including valid submissions, missing required fields, and error submissions.","Exclude employee test submissions from business reports when possible.","Date changes to forms, content, or campaigns to read metrics in context.","Only compare stages with equivalent recognition and conditions.","Review data collection by purpose, access rights, and applicable obligations."]},{type:"p",text:"Don't conclude a site's effectiveness from just one week of data or comparing periods with different seasons. Take a look at trends, quality requirements, and changes made. The article [measuring websites using GA4 and Search Console](/blog/do-luong-website-ga4-search-console) guides how to view tool data; This article helps choose which business questions to ask first."},{type:"callout",variant:"warn",title:"Not every metric is a target",text:"Time on page, views or rankings can help diagnose problems, but don't automatically translate to revenue. Place them next to customer actions and business results."}],faq:[{question:"What is the most important index of a business website?",answer:"Depends on website role. Choose the metric closest to your goal, such as qualified consultation requests, orders, appointments, or process processing time."},{question:"Can a website with few visits be effective?",answer:"Maybe, if the visitor is targeted correctly and produces valuable results. Need to look at quality and journeys instead of just looking at total visits."},{question:"Do I need to install GA4 to measure everything?",answer:"GA4 can support web behavior tracking, but businesses still need to define events, examine data, and hook into the right sales process."}]},{slug:"website-trong-hanh-trinh-khach-hang-doanh-nghiep",title:"Where is the website located in the business's customer journey?",metaTitle:"The role of websites in the business customer journey | Xartisan Studio",description:"Design the website along the journey from research, appraisal, comparison to contact and back, so that each page supports a customer decision.",keywords:["website in the customer journey","corporate sales support website","customer journey on the website","Website design according to customers"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Customers","Journey","Content"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Visitors rarely decide after just one page view. The website needs to help them find the right answer at each stage and help the team continue the conversation when they are ready.",visual:"journey",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","viet-noi-dung-website","website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"A business customer might hear about the company from an acquaintance, Google the name, read the project, send the page to a colleague, and then come back a few days later. The website does not necessarily close the transaction immediately; it needs to help the visitor move forward through each question and create a clear connection with the team."},{type:"h2",text:"Four stages guests usually go through"},{type:"table",headers:["Phase","Questions in the guest's mind","Website content should be available"],rows:[["Explore","What does this company do? Is it right for my needs?","Clear message, service group, service industry and operating area."],["Appraisal","Have they done the same thing? Who is responsible?","Projects have context, scope, implementation roles, and authentic contact information."],["Compare","What are the different scopes, methods, costs and risks?","Process, selection criteria, frequently asked questions and cooperation conditions."],["Contact","What information do I need to send to receive proper advice?","Short forms, clear contact channels, and transparent response expectations."]]},{type:"h2",text:"Each page should have a clear mission"},{type:"p",text:"The homepage helps customers quickly identify the business and choose a direction. The service page explains the problem, scope and how to do it. The project page provides evidence, while the contact page helps start the conversation. If every page repeats the same general introduction and call-to-action, it will be difficult for visitors to know what to read next."},{type:"p",text:"The form should also ask for the right amount of information. A request for a quote may require the type of service, scale, or estimated time; Asking too much the first time makes customers hesitate to send, asking too little makes the team have to ask again from the beginning. After the customer sends, the internal reception process needs someone to follow up."},{type:"h2",text:"Illustrate the journey of a B2B customer"},{type:"p",text:"A company looking to build a dealer portal might start with a question about how to distribute documents. The person in charge then looks at the service page to understand the scope, reads about projects that are close to their industry, passes the link to the IT department, and then submits the request. If the service page only talks about technology, the project page doesn't give context, and the form doesn't ask about user groups, the customer has to piece together the pieces of information themselves or ask again from the beginning."},{type:"table",headers:["Signals from guests","Support point on website","What the team needs to do next"],rows:[["Read the solutions page","Clearly state the user group, problem and appropriate scope.","Prepare questions to discover needs, not assuming the customer has already made a decision."],["View projects or profiles","Describe the context, implementation and limitations of public information.","Verify whether the request is similar to a previous project or requires different capabilities."],["Submit form","Ask for enough information to route the request, clearly indicating the next response step.","Assign people in charge, respond according to internal deadlines, and update statuses."],["Come back in a few days","Keep content easy to find and links consistent across devices.","Continue to exchange as needed; do not consider new visits as consent to receive marketing."]]},{type:"p",text:"Real life journeys rarely follow a straight line. Decision makers, users, and technical reviewers may need different evidence; a guest may also return multiple times before being ready. So, interview both salespeople and customers who have agreed to share their experiences, then use the language they actually use to organize the page and frequently asked questions."},{type:"h2",text:"Check the connection between website and people"},{type:"ul",items:["Each important page has a suitable next step, without forcing visitors to use the same call-to-action.","The form has a recipient, a backup plan, and a clear message when sending fails.","The team knows which requests the customer has viewed without inferring that they have agreed to provide data beyond the stated purpose.","Responses in the consultation are returned to the website when appropriate and approved for content."]},{type:"ul",items:["Each important page has a suitable next step, without forcing visitors to use the same call-to-action.","The form has a recipient, a backup plan, and a clear message when sending fails.","The team knows which requests the customer has viewed without inferring that they have agreed to provide data beyond the stated purpose.","Responses in the consultation are returned to the website when appropriate and approved for content.","Track request type, not just button presses; View responses from reception staff to detect missing questions."]},{type:"p",text:"Organizing content according to the journey helps the website both represent the brand and support the business. See more [how to write website content for customers to trust and contact](/blog/viet-noi-dung-website) and [business website structure](/blog/website-doanh-nghiep-can-nhung-trang-gi)."}],faq:[{question:"Can a website replace a sales staff?",answer:"Websites help customers research and send requests, but consulting, negotiating and building relationships often still require the right team."},{question:"Does every website page need a contact button?",answer:"There should be a path appropriate to the page content. The project page can lead to communication about capabilities; The manual page may lead to related services."},{question:"How do you know if the customer journey on the website is broken?",answer:"See drop-offs, error forms, repeated questions in consultations, and pages with lots of views but no follow-up action."}]},{slug:"website-rieng-va-cac-kenh-so-doanh-nghiep",title:"Why do businesses need their own website besides social networks?",metaTitle:"Private website and social network: do businesses need both? | Xartisan Studio",description:"Websites and social networks do two different things. Learn how to use the website as an information platform controlled by the business, while social networks support access and dialogue.",keywords:["private website for businesses","websites and social networks","own a business website","business digital channel"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Ownership channel","Brand","Digital strategy"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Social networks are useful for reaching out and interacting, while websites help businesses organize official information, master content structure and build their own journey on their domain name.",visual:"channel",ctaService:"/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","doanh-nghiep-can-so-huu-gi-sau-khi-lam-website","tam-nhin-website-doanh-nghiep-trong-3-nam"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Social networks help businesses appear where customers are spending their time. Websites help businesses organize information according to their logic, maintain an official address and direct customers to appropriate actions. The two channels complement each other; Choosing one and abandoning the other often results in a loss of different possibilities."},{type:"h2",text:"Differences in control and organization of information"},{type:"table",headers:["Business website","Social network"],rows:[["Businesses proactively structure their pages, content, domains, and contact journeys.","Content and display follow the platform's format, tools, and rules."],["Suitable for explaining services, storing documents, projects and official policies.","Great for quick updates, dialogue, and content distribution to followers."],["Can organize links between content, services, forms, and measurement tools.","You can bring visitors to your website or create an exchange right on the platform."],["Need to invest in construction, maintenance, content and account protection.","Depends on platform accessibility, features and accounts."]]},{type:"h2",text:"Design how the two channels lead to each other"},{type:"p",text:"A post can introduce a new story or update, then lead readers to the appropriate service page, project profile, or form on the website. Conversely, the website can lead to active social channels for customers to continue following or interacting. Brand names, contact information and messaging should be consistent so customers don't encounter different versions of the same business."},{type:"h2",text:"For example, one content can go through many channels"},{type:"p",text:"Let's say the team has a test guide before choosing warehouse management software. The full version on the website can explain the criteria, limitations and questions to ask the supplier; social media post stating a short idea with a link; Emails to existing customers can lead to a downloadable checklist if they are evaluating a solution. Each version does something different but points to the main source of information, update date and contact point."},{type:"ol",items:["Choose a real customer question and determine who in the business has experience answering it.","Publish the full version on your website with title, update date and link to relevant service where appropriate.","Create shortened content for each channel, avoid posting verbatim without adding context.","Assign consistent campaign IDs to links to distinguish traffic sources in measurement tools.","Check for feedback and new questions; Update the original page if core information has changed."]},{type:"p",text:"This approach does not turn the website into a place where the business owns all customer relationships or data. Social platforms still have their own rules, and personal data should only be collected according to the announced purpose and necessary permissions. The value of a website lies in the fact that businesses have better control over their address, structure and content, and can create clear lines between touch points."},{type:"p",text:"To start, a business can choose a flagship service, a frequently asked customer question, and a consistently active social channel. During the first month, publish a full explainer page on your website, create some short content that leads back to that page, include a contact source, and ask your sales team if it's easier for customers to find the information. After the testing round, decide whether to increase frequency, add formats or invest in other channels. This helps avoid having a large multi-channel plan but no one to maintain it."},{type:"p",text:"Personal data should not be collected just because it can be done. Every form should clearly state its intended purpose, protect access rights, and comply with the obligations applicable to the business. Websites are channels organized by businesses, but collecting and using data still requires responsibility."},{type:"h2",text:"Start your own website from the core"},{type:"ul",items:["Use a domain name that the business controls and has someone in charge of renewing it.","Upload official information, key services, and verified proof of competency.","Set a primary action like call, send request, or schedule.","Drive social content to the right landing page, instead of just to the home page.","Track contact sources to see which channels provide appropriate customer support."]},{type:"p",text:"For sales businesses, the choice between a platform and a separate website depends on the category, operations and order control needs; See [comparison article for sale on the floor and separate website](/blog/ban-tren-san-hay-lam-website-rieng). With a business website, start from [objective and appropriate structure](/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep)."}],faq:[{question:"If there is a social network, does a business need a website?",answer:"Websites are still useful when businesses need an official address, present information in a unique structure, keep records and connect contact processes."},{question:"Does the website ensure that the business will own all customer data?",answer:"Are not. Data collection and use is subject to design, third-party tools, customer consent, and applicable obligations. It is necessary to clearly define what data is saved and who controls it."},{question:"Should I prioritize creating a website or social network first?",answer:"Depends on current situation and goals. Businesses can build a core information foundation on the website and then use social channels for distribution and dialogue."}]},{slug:"noi-dung-website-la-tai-san-tich-luy",title:"How can website content become a cumulative asset?",metaTitle:"Website content is a cumulative asset Xartisan Studio",description:"Build a website content warehouse from customer questions, projects and business experiences; Update, link, and measure so content continues to be useful over time.",keywords:["corporate website content","Website content is asset","Build SEO content","Website content management"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Content","SEO","Accumulate"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Articles are valuable not only on the day they are posted. When derived from real experience, properly linked and updated when needed, content helps customers understand the business and helps the team reuse knowledge.",visual:"content",ctaService:"/dich-vu-seo-website",related:["viet-noi-dung-website","website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","do-luong-hieu-qua-website-bang-ket-qua-kinh-doanh"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Businesses often have a wealth of knowledge scattered across consulting calls, sales documents, support questions, and the experience of veteran personnel. When compiled into clear website content, that knowledge can help visitors answer their own questions and help teams reuse it consistently."},{type:"h2",text:"Cumulative content starts from real experiences"},{type:"p",text:"A useful article can explain the process, selection criteria, common risks, or situations the business has dealt with. These topics differentiate themselves from articles that simply change keywords and repeat common information. Ask sales and customer service staff what customers often wonder about before making a decision."},{type:"h2",text:"Build a structured content repository"},{type:"ol",items:["Group questions by need group, service, and decision-making stage.","Choose a main page that explains the service or overview topic.","Write supporting articles that go deeper into each question, each article addressing a clear intention.","Link support articles to the main page and related articles so readers have a way forward.","Record the person in charge, the source of information, and the review date for each article."]},{type:"h2",text:"Illustration of a content cluster for a website making service"},{type:"p",text:"If customers often ask how to choose a website builder, businesses can create a main page explaining the scope of design, development and delivery. The support articles go into depth about what is needed after handover, how to prepare content, questions to clarify before quoting, how to accept, and how to operate after launch. Each content answers a specific need, leads to the main page when readers need to learn about the service, and is horizontally linked when the two topics are truly complementary."},{type:"table",headers:["Components of the job assignment","Questions need answering"],rows:[["Readers and situations","Whoever reads this article, what do they need to decide?"],["Main question","What specific question will the article address, how to avoid duplication of existing pages?"],["Original material","Are there any interviews, procedures, examples, photos or internal documents that are allowed?"],["Responsible person","Who verifies professional details, who reviews commercial information and claims?"],["The road continues","Which pages should readers read, whom should they contact, or what steps should they take after the article?"],["Review plan","What information is subject to change and what events require early updates?"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Content needs to be managed after posting"},{type:"p",text:"Accumulation doesn't mean posting as much as possible. Check to see if the information is correct, if the links work, if the article serves the right question, and if any content is competing with another page on the same website. When updating, it is necessary to change the substantive content and record the correct date of correction with the work done."},{type:"ul",items:["Group or differentiate articles that answer the same search intent; Don't keep multiple pages that are nearly identical just to target keyword variations.","Update prices, processes, project photos, product names and contact information when there are genuine changes.","Check internal links, external links, forms and display on the phone after editing.","Track search impressions and helpful actions; Do not delete content just because there have been no visits for a short period of time.","Save the source, reviewer, and reason for the update so the next team can understand why the information was written the way it was."]},{type:"p",text:"Google recommends prioritizing content that is useful, trustworthy, and created for readers; Using AI tools to create multiple pages that lack value may violate the large-scale content abuse policy. See [Google Search Central's helpful content guide](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/creating-helpful-content) and [how to write website content for clients](/blog/viet-noi-dung-website)."},{type:"callout",variant:"tip",title:"A test before posting",text:"If visitors have read this article, what more specific things do they understand, and what experience or evidence does the business have to be responsible for that content? If you can't answer, please add real material before publishing."},{type:"p",text:"Good content not only helps the website express its professional voice, but also creates a natural path to the appropriate service. See [website SEO service](/dich-vu-seo-website) to learn how to structure, optimize and track content for each website."}],faq:[{question:"Can website articles bring in visitors forever?",answer:"No content guarantees traffic or customers forever. Content can continue to be useful if it remains accurate, meets needs, and is operated well by the website."},{question:"How many articles should I post per month?",answer:"There is no universal frequency suitable for all businesses. Choose a schedule where the team can maintain quality, genuine experience and updates."},{question:"Should we use AI to write SEO articles?",answer:"AI can be used to research or organize ideas, but someone needs to be responsible for checking accuracy, adding their own experience, and ensuring the article is useful to readers."}]},{slug:"su-menh-tam-nhin-xartisan-studio-website-la-tai-san",title:"Xartisan Studio mission: for businesses to own websites as an asset",metaTitle:"Xartisan Studio mission and vision for business websites",description:"Xartisan Studio pursues the goal of changing the way businesses view websites: from a one-time expense into an asset in the business's name, protected, preserved and developed.",keywords:["Xartisan Studio mission","Xartisan Studio vision","Website is an asset","Xartisan Studio designs business websites"],category:"Xartisan Studio & orientation",tags:["Mission","Vision","Brand"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"Why does Xartisan Studio say websites are assets? The article shares brand orientation, working methods and commitments for businesses to be proactive with their digital platforms.",visual:"mission",ctaService:"/gioi-thieu",related:["website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep","doanh-nghiep-can-so-huu-gi-sau-khi-lam-website","van-hanh-website-nhu-mot-tai-san"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Many websites are invested carefully before launch but lack people to take care of them afterward. Expired domain names, old content, administrative rights are outside the business and no one knows if the website is generating contacts or not. Xartisan Studio chooses a different perspective: the website should be an asset in the name of the business, which can be controlled and continued to develop."},{type:"h2",text:"Mission: change the way businesses look at websites"},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio's purpose is to transform a website from a one-time expense into an asset that is built on the right foundation, protected, preserved and developed to support business activities. That starts with understanding the customer's goals and journey, rather than just choosing a theme and then throwing in content."},{type:"h2",text:"Vision to 2030"},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio aims to become a unit where Vietnamese small and medium business owners believe in handing over their website like an asset - where each website is evaluated by the customers and revenue it brings, not by the number of pages or beauty. This is the orientation for Xartisan Studio to organize its way of working; it is not a commitment that every website will generate a fixed level of revenue."},{type:"h2",text:"Five principles in how Xartisan Studio works"},{type:"ol",items:["**Build the right foundation**: clarify your goals, customers, and buying journey before finalizing the scope.","**Grant ownership rights**: domain names, data, administrative accounts and source code scope are unified for businesses to be proactive.","**Protection and preservation**: have someone to monitor, back up and handle incidents according to the operating agreement.","**Asset development**: content, SEO and conversion optimization based on needs and actual data.","**Transparent reporting**: clearly distinguish between work done, observed data and business results."]},{type:"h2",text:"Orientation is only meaningful when translated into work"},{type:"table",headers:["Orientation","Shown in the project","What customers can check"],rows:[["Website is the asset of the business","Unify naming rights, administrative rights, data and source code scope in the handover contract.","Who holds the domain name, how the business logs in, and what documents are handed over."],["Build a foundation according to your goals","Survey users, processes, content, integration and acceptance criteria before finalizing the solution.","Are the required records, scope of work and inspection criteria agreed upon?"],["Long-term protection and development","Unify responsibilities for backups, updates, troubleshooting, and improvement roadmaps.","Who does each job, how often, are there any limitations or costs to know."],["Measured by actual value","Choose a tracking method that fits your goals and report the limits of your data.","Where do the data come from, how are they defined and what cannot be concluded?"]]},{type:"p",text:"This is also how a business can evaluate a vendor: ask them to explain who holds the account, how the contract ends, the backup process, the scope of support, and how to validate results. The answers should appear in the proposal or agreement, not just in the introduction. Xartisan Studio's unique qualities need to be seen through specific decisions and handovers in each project."},{type:"h2",text:"What Xartisan Studio needs to clarify is the commitment limit"},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio can commit to the scope of work, delivery standards, coordination, technical responsibilities in the agreement and reporting. Revenue, search rankings or number of visitors also depend on the market, product, price, content, budget and how the team receives requests. Therefore, the vision towards evaluating websites by business value does not mean guaranteeing a fixed result for every customer."},{type:"p",text:"Xartisan Studio does not commit to a fixed revenue number or ranking. The team agrees on the tasks, measurements and scope before starting, then clearly reports what the website is doing. This is the difference between a brand promise and a customer-auditable process: from survey questions, proposal scope, deliverables to post-implementation reporting."},{type:"h2",text:"What questions can customers check for that unique quality?"},{type:"ul",items:["Who owns the domain name, admin account and measurement tools after the project is completed?","Which goals are prioritized and which acceptance criteria are agreed upon in writing?","When scope, maintenance or third-party service issues arise, how are costs and responsibilities communicated?","The report separates what was done, what data was observed, and how the results depend on the market?","After handover, who is the focal point when the business needs to update, handle errors or evaluate the next development step?"]},{type:"p",text:"These questions apply to any developer and help businesses choose partners on a clear basis. Learn more about [Xartisan Studio](/gioi-thieu), [business website design service](/thiet-ke-website-doanh-nghiep) and [website operating model](/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website)."}],faq:[{question:"What is Xartisan Studio's mission?",answer:"Xartisan Studio aims to change the way business owners view websites: from a one-time expense to an asset in the name of the business, protected, preserved and developed to support business."},{question:"What is Xartisan Studio's vision to 2030?",answer:"Become a unit where Vietnamese small and medium-sized business owners trust their websites like they are an asset, and together with customers, evaluate their websites through actual business value."},{question:"Does Xartisan Studio commit to website revenue?",answer:"Do not commit to a fixed revenue number. Xartisan Studio unifies the scope of work, KPIs appropriate to the project and reports transparently based on measurable data."}]},{slug:"tong-chi-phi-so-huu-website-3-nam",title:"Total cost of website ownership for 3 years: what do businesses need to calculate?",metaTitle:"Total cost of website ownership in 3 years | Xartisan Studio",description:"The design fee is only a part. The framework for calculating the total cost of website ownership helps businesses estimate operations, licenses, personnel, maintenance, and transferability over three years.",keywords:["total cost of website ownership","Website cost for 3 years","Business website operating costs","Long-term website creation costs"],category:"Website assets",tags:["Life cycle costs","Operations","Budget"],date:"2026-10-12",readingMinutes:6,excerpt:"To compare two website building options, look at the total costs over the expected period of use: from construction, renewal and operating personnel to maintenance, upgrades and switching suppliers.",visual:"phases",ctaService:"/bang-gia-thiet-ke-website",related:["ngan-sach-website-nam-dau","chi-phi-thiet-ke-website","website-la-tai-san-so-cua-doanh-nghiep"],blocks:[{type:"p",text:"Two website quotes may differ significantly but are not necessarily in the same range. One side may include just design and programming; The other party can include content import, administration instructions, backups, error tracking, and post-run support. To make long-term decisions, businesses should look at the total cost of ownership over the expected period of use, instead of just comparing the initial figure."},{type:"h2",text:"What does the total cost of ownership include?"},{type:"p",text:"Total cost of ownership, often called TCO, is the total cost required to put the website into use, maintain it, and change as business needs evolve. TCO does not predict how much revenue the website will bring in; It helps businesses know what resources they need to invest in order for the website to operate in reality."},{type:"table",headers:["Cost group","Examples need to be included in the estimate","Questions to check scope"],rows:[["Initial construction","Survey, design, programming, data entry, integration and testing.","How many page templates, business flows, edits and data entry does the quote include?"],["Periodic infrastructure","Domain, server, email, file hosting, certificate or notification service.","Who is in charge, what usage is charged and how does the renewal fee change?"],["Software and third parties","Paid plugins, fonts, libraries, APIs, payment gateways or analytics tools.","Who owns the license, can it be renewed annually or on a per-use basis, can it be replaced?"],["Operational personnel","Time to update content, review information, process requests and review data.","Which department does it, how much time is spent each month and what training is needed?"],["Maintenance and development","Prioritize backups, updates, fixes, security testing, and enhancements.","What is included in the warranty, what is scheduled maintenance or charged separately?"],["Convert or terminate","Export data, hand over accounts, switch servers, change providers.","Under what conditions can businesses receive data back and continue operating?"]]},{type:"h2",text:"Simple budgeting formula for 36 months"},{type:"p",text:"The calculation table can be made according to the formula: initial construction costs + total recurring fees for 36 months + internal personnel costs + expected maintenance or upgrades + conversion costs, if any. For services based on usage, write down current usage, threshold and how to monitor; Don't multiply a fixed amount over three years if the contract allows for changes based on traffic."},{type:"ol",items:["Record each payment according to the payment cycle: one time, monthly, annually or according to usage.","Separate confirmed costs from estimates; state the assumption and who needs confirmation.","Factor staffing time into planning, even without invoices from vendors.","Create base and growth scenarios, such as adding languages, products or traffic.","Review your budget every quarter or when scope changes, instead of assuming all fees stay the same."]},{type:"h2",text:"Compare two quotes on the same premises"},{type:"p",text:"Suppose option A has low construction costs but the business writes its own content, imports products, sets up tracking and handles updates. Option B has a higher initial fee but includes those tasks and instructions. It is impossible to conclude which option is cheaper without evaluating internal time, output quality, extensions and post-handover support. Creating a parallel range table will show which accounts are empty instead of just looking at the total amount."},{type:"p",text:"In particular, it is necessary to distinguish defect warranty from regular maintenance. Warranty usually covers errors within the scope of acceptance; Content updates, version upgrades, ongoing monitoring or new feature development can be other tasks. Specific conditions depend on the contract, technology and agreement of both parties, so please request a written description."},{type:"h2",text:"From cost estimates to investment decisions"},{type:"p",text:"After knowing the total cost, consider the role of the website: does it help customers evaluate capacity, receive requests, make sales or reduce internal operations? Choose a few observable outcomes, like appropriate requests being received, processing times reduced, or staff updating content without having to wait for the supplier. Compare over time to understand whether the investment level is consistent with the value and performance; Don't turn your estimate into a revenue promise."},{type:"ul",items:["Ask for a list of delivery scope, recurring payments, and third-party services.","Confirm ownership rights and process for renewing domain names, servers, and licenses.","Ask how incurred costs are notified and approved.","Check out how to export data, get source code under contract, and transfer to another provider.","Only choose an operating level that the business has people in charge of and a budget to maintain."]},{type:"p",text:"If you are preparing an initial budget, see [how to allocate the first year website budget](/blog/ngan-sach-website-nam-dau), [items in website design costs](/blog/chi-phi-thiet-ke-website) and [terms needed in the contract](/blog/hop-dong-thiet-ke-website). Websites are considered manageable assets when businesses understand both maintenance costs and post-handover control."}],faq:[{question:"Is the cost of owning a website just hosting and domain fees?",answer:"Are not. There are also construction costs, licensing, personnel updates, maintenance, upgrades, and sometimes data or vendor migration."},{question:"Is it possible to know the exact cost of a website in three years from the beginning?",answer:"It's possible to budget for known amounts and make assumptions about usage, but traffic-based fees, business changes, or expansion plans can change total costs."},{question:"Is the website with the lowest TCO the best option?",answer:"Not necessarily. Need to compare the same scope, quality, ownership, operability and value of the website that needs to support the business."}]}];export{n as b};
